DATA.push({"c":"toeic","l":3,"w":[["scaffolding","/ˈskæfəldɪŋ/","n.","鷹架","Scaffolding covers the front of the building.","大樓正面搭滿了鷹架。"],["excavate","/ˈekskəveɪt/","v.","開挖","The crew will excavate the site for the foundation.","施工團隊將開挖地基。"],["bulldozer","/ˈbʊldoʊzər/","n.","推土機","A bulldozer cleared the land for the new mall.","推土機為新購物中心整地。"],["demolish","/dɪˈmɑːlɪʃ/","v.","拆除","The old warehouse will be demolished next month.","舊倉庫下個月將被拆除。"],["demolition","/ˌdeməˈlɪʃn/","n.","拆除","Demolition of the old wing begins on Monday.","舊側翼大樓的拆除工程週一開始。"],["tear down","/ˌter ˈdaʊn/","phr.","拆掉","They tore down the old parking structure.","他們拆掉了舊的立體停車場。"],["put up","/ˌpʊt ˈʌp/","phr.","搭建；張貼","Workers are putting up a temporary fence.","工人正在搭設臨時圍籬。"],["break ground","/ˌbreɪk ˈɡraʊnd/","phr.","動土、開工","The company will break ground on the new plant in May.","公司將於五月為新廠動土。"],["groundbreaking","/ˈɡraʊndbreɪkɪŋ/","adj./n.","開創性的；動土典禮","The mayor attended the groundbreaking ceremony.","市長出席了動土典禮。"],["pave","/peɪv/","v.","鋪（路）","The city will pave the road next to our office.","市政府將為我們辦公室旁的道路鋪柏油。"],["finishing touches","/ˈfɪnɪʃɪŋ ˌtʌtʃɪz/","phr.","最後修飾","Painters are adding the finishing touches to the lobby.","油漆工正在為大廳做最後的修飾。"],["laborer","/ˈleɪbərər/","n.","勞工","The firm hired fifty laborers for the project.","公司為這項工程僱用了五十名工人。"],["civil engineer","/ˌsɪvl ˌendʒɪˈnɪr/","phr.","土木工程師","A civil engineer inspected the bridge.","一位土木工程師檢查了這座橋。"],["architectural","/ˌɑːrkɪˈtektʃərəl/","adj.","建築的","The building won an architectural award.","這棟建築獲得建築獎項。"],["building permit","/ˈbɪldɪŋ ˌpɜːrmɪt/","phr.","建築執照","We are still waiting for the building permit.","我們還在等建築執照。"],["building code","/ˈbɪldɪŋ koʊd/","phr.","建築法規","The renovation must meet local building codes.","翻修工程必須符合當地建築法規。"],["structural","/ˈstrʌktʃərəl/","adj.","結構的","Engineers found no structural damage after the earthquake.","工程師在地震後未發現結構損壞。"],["foundation","/faʊnˈdeɪʃn/","n.","地基；基金會；基礎","Cracks appeared in the building's foundation.","大樓地基出現裂縫。"],["beam","/biːm/","n.","樑","Steel beams support the roof.","鋼樑支撐著屋頂。"],["insulation","/ˌɪnsəˈleɪʃn/","n.","隔熱、絕緣材料","Better insulation will lower our heating costs.","更好的隔熱能降低暖氣費用。"],["duct","/dʌkt/","n.","管道、導管","The air ducts are cleaned twice a year.","空調風管每年清潔兩次。"],["HVAC","/ˈeɪtʃ væk/","n.","暖通空調系統","The HVAC system will be replaced this summer.","空調系統將在今年夏天更換。"],["upkeep","/ˈʌpkiːp/","n.","保養、維護（費）","The tenant pays for the upkeep of the garden.","房客負擔花園的維護費用。"],["dilapidated","/dɪˈlæpɪdeɪtɪd/","adj.","破舊失修的","The dilapidated building was finally restored.","那棟破舊的建築終於修復了。"],["restoration","/ˌrestəˈreɪʃn/","n.","修復、恢復","The restoration of the old theater took two years.","老劇院的修復工程花了兩年。"],["modernization","/ˌmɑːdərnəˈzeɪʃn/","n.","現代化","The modernization of the factory cost millions.","工廠的現代化耗資數百萬。"],["system failure","/ˈsɪstəm ˌfeɪljər/","phr.","系統故障","A system failure delayed all online orders.","系統故障導致所有線上訂單延誤。"],["servicing","/ˈsɜːrvɪsɪŋ/","n.","保養、維修服務","The copier is due for servicing next week.","影印機下週該保養了。"],["off-site","/ˌɔːf ˈsaɪt/","adj./adv.","場外的、異地的","Backup data is stored off-site.","備份資料存放在異地。"],["restore power","/rɪˌstɔːr ˈpaʊər/","phr.","恢復供電","Crews are working to restore power to the area.","工作人員正在努力恢復該區供電。"],["conserve","/kənˈsɜːrv/","v.","節約、保存","Please conserve water during the drought.","乾旱期間請節約用水。"],["toner cartridge","/ˈtoʊnər ˌkɑːrtrɪdʒ/","phr.","碳粉匣","Replace the toner cartridge when the light flashes.","指示燈閃爍時請更換碳粉匣。"],["refill","/ˌriːˈfɪl/","v./n.","補充、再裝滿","Please refill the paper tray when it's empty.","紙匣空了請補紙。"],["paper tray","/ˈpeɪpər treɪ/","phr.","紙匣","Load more paper into the paper tray.","請在紙匣裡多放些紙。"],["double-sided","/ˌdʌbl ˈsaɪdɪd/","adj.","雙面的","Please print double-sided to save paper.","請雙面列印以節省紙張。"],["encrypt","/ɪnˈkrɪpt/","v.","加密","All customer data is encrypted for security.","所有客戶資料都經過加密以確保安全。"],["firewall","/ˈfaɪərwɔːl/","n.","防火牆","The firewall blocks unauthorized access to our network.","防火牆阻擋未經授權存取我們的網路。"],["malware","/ˈmælwer/","n.","惡意軟體","Don't open attachments that may contain malware.","不要打開可能含有惡意軟體的附件。"],["antivirus software","/ˌæntiˈvaɪrəs ˌsɔːftwer/","phr.","防毒軟體","Antivirus software is installed on every computer.","每台電腦都安裝了防毒軟體。"],["hacker","/ˈhækər/","n.","駭客","Hackers tried to access the company's database.","駭客試圖入侵公司資料庫。"],["data breach","/ˈdeɪtə briːtʃ/","phr.","資料外洩","The data breach affected thousands of customers.","資料外洩影響了數千名顧客。"],["security breach","/sɪˈkjʊrəti briːtʃ/","phr.","安全漏洞、資安事件","Report any security breach to IT immediately.","任何資安事件請立即通報資訊部。"],["security patch","/sɪˈkjʊrəti pætʃ/","phr.","安全修補程式","Install the security patch as soon as possible.","請儘快安裝安全性修補程式。"],["vulnerability","/ˌvʌlnərəˈbɪləti/","n.","弱點、漏洞","The audit found a vulnerability in our system.","稽核發現了我們系統的一個漏洞。"],["cybersecurity","/ˌsaɪbərsɪˈkjʊrəti/","n.","網路安全、資安","We hired a cybersecurity expert last month.","我們上個月聘請了一位資安專家。"],["phishing","/ˈfɪʃɪŋ/","n.","網路釣魚","Be careful of phishing emails asking for passwords.","小心要求提供密碼的釣魚郵件。"],["identity theft","/aɪˈdentəti θeft/","phr.","身分盜用","Shred documents to prevent identity theft.","把文件絞碎以防身分盜用。"],["authenticate","/ɔːˈθentɪkeɪt/","v.","驗證、認證","Users must authenticate with a code sent to their phone.","使用者須用傳到手機的驗證碼進行驗證。"],["two-factor","/ˌtuː ˈfæktər/","adj.","雙重（驗證）的","We require two-factor authentication for all accounts.","所有帳號都須使用雙重驗證。"],["password-protected","/ˈpæswɜːrd prəˌtektɪd/","adj.","有密碼保護的","The salary file is password-protected.","薪資檔案有密碼保護。"],["unauthorized","/ʌnˈɔːθəraɪzd/","adj.","未經授權的","Unauthorized personnel may not enter the server room.","未經授權人員不得進入伺服器機房。"],["access control","/ˈækses kənˌtroʊl/","phr.","門禁管制；存取控制","The new access control system uses fingerprints.","新的門禁系統使用指紋辨識。"],["security clearance","/sɪˈkjʊrəti ˌklɪrəns/","phr.","安全許可","Only staff with security clearance can enter.","只有具安全許可的員工能進入。"],["biometric","/ˌbaɪoʊˈmetrɪk/","adj.","生物辨識的","Biometric scanners were installed at the entrance.","入口裝設了生物辨識掃描器。"],["surveillance camera","/sərˈveɪləns ˌkæmərə/","phr.","監視器","Surveillance cameras record the parking area.","監視器錄下停車區的畫面。"],["footage","/ˈfʊtɪdʒ/","n.","（影片）畫面、片段","Security reviewed the camera footage from last night.","保全調閱了昨晚的監視器畫面。"],["motion sensor","/ˈmoʊʃn ˌsensər/","phr.","動作感應器","The lights are controlled by motion sensors.","燈光由動作感應器控制。"],["patrol","/pəˈtroʊl/","v./n.","巡邏","Guards patrol the building every two hours.","警衛每兩小時巡邏大樓一次。"],["escort","/ɪˈskɔːrt/","v.","陪同、護送","Visitors must be escorted at all times.","訪客須全程有人陪同。"],["restricted area","/rɪˌstrɪktɪd ˈeriə/","phr.","管制區","This is a restricted area for authorized staff only.","此為管制區，僅限授權人員進入。"],["remote access","/rɪˌmoʊt ˈækses/","phr.","遠端存取","Employees have remote access to the company network.","員工可遠端存取公司網路。"],["remotely","/rɪˈmoʊtli/","adv.","遠端地","IT fixed my laptop remotely.","資訊部遠端修好了我的筆電。"],["bandwidth","/ˈbændwɪdθ/","n.","頻寬；（個人）處理能力","Video calls use a lot of bandwidth.","視訊通話會佔用大量頻寬。"],["connectivity","/ˌkɑːnekˈtɪvəti/","n.","連線能力","The hotel offers excellent connectivity for business travelers.","飯店為商務旅客提供絕佳的網路連線。"],["compatibility","/kəmˌpætəˈbɪləti/","n.","相容性","Check the software's compatibility with your system.","請確認軟體與您系統的相容性。"],["compatible with","/kəmˈpætəbl wɪð/","phr.","與……相容","This printer is compatible with all our laptops.","這台印表機與我們所有筆電相容。"],["configuration","/kənˌfɪɡjəˈreɪʃn/","n.","設定、配置","The network configuration was changed last night.","網路設定昨晚被變更了。"],["unresponsive","/ˌʌnrɪˈspɑːnsɪv/","adj.","無回應的","The program became unresponsive and had to be closed.","程式沒有回應，只好關閉。"],["corrupted","/kəˈrʌptɪd/","adj.","（檔案）損毀的","The file is corrupted and cannot be opened.","這個檔案損毀了，無法開啟。"],["data recovery","/ˈdeɪtə rɪˌkʌvəri/","phr.","資料救援","A data recovery service retrieved the lost files.","資料救援服務找回了遺失的檔案。"],["data center","/ˈdeɪtə ˌsentər/","phr.","資料中心","The company is building a new data center.","公司正在興建新的資料中心。"],["cloud computing","/ˈklaʊd kəmˌpjuːtɪŋ/","phr.","雲端運算","Cloud computing has reduced our IT costs.","雲端運算降低了我們的資訊成本。"],["streaming","/ˈstriːmɪŋ/","n.","串流","The keynote will be available via live streaming.","主題演講將透過直播串流提供。"],["peripheral","/pəˈrɪfərəl/","n./adj.","周邊設備；周邊的","Printers and scanners are common computer peripherals.","印表機和掃描器是常見的電腦周邊。"],["processor","/ˈprɑːsesər/","n.","處理器","The new model has a faster processor.","新機型有更快的處理器。"],["tech-savvy","/ˌtek ˈsævi/","adj.","精通科技的","We are looking for a tech-savvy assistant.","我們正在找一位熟悉科技的助理。"],["computer literate","/kəmˌpjuːtər ˈlɪtərət/","phr.","會使用電腦的","All applicants must be computer literate.","所有應徵者都必須會使用電腦。"],["migration","/maɪˈɡreɪʃn/","n.","（資料、系統）轉移","The data migration will take place over the weekend.","資料轉移將在週末進行。"],["integration","/ˌɪntɪˈɡreɪʃn/","n.","整合","Integration with our accounting software is easy.","與我們的會計軟體整合很容易。"],["network administrator","/ˈnetwɜːrk ədˌmɪnɪstreɪtər/","phr.","網路管理員","Ask the network administrator to reset your access.","請網路管理員重設您的存取權限。"],["developer","/dɪˈveləpər/","n.","開發人員；開發商","Our developers are testing the new app.","我們的開發人員正在測試新 App。"],["algorithm","/ˈælɡərɪðəm/","n.","演算法","The algorithm recommends products to customers.","演算法會向顧客推薦產品。"],["analytics","/ˌænəˈlɪtɪks/","n.","分析（數據）","Web analytics show where our visitors come from.","網站分析顯示訪客來自哪裡。"],["machine learning","/məˌʃiːn ˈlɜːrnɪŋ/","phr.","機器學習","The company uses machine learning to detect fraud.","公司利用機器學習來偵測詐騙。"],["virtual reality","/ˌvɜːrtʃuəl riˈæləti/","phr.","虛擬實境","Trainees practice safety procedures in virtual reality.","受訓人員在虛擬實境中練習安全程序。"],["digitize","/ˈdɪdʒɪtaɪz/","v.","數位化","We are digitizing all our paper records.","我們正把所有紙本紀錄數位化。"],["paperless","/ˈpeɪpərləs/","adj.","無紙化的","The office went paperless last year.","辦公室去年實施無紙化。"],["innovate","/ˈɪnəveɪt/","v.","創新","Companies must innovate to stay competitive.","企業必須創新才能保持競爭力。"],["pioneer","/ˌpaɪəˈnɪr/","n./v.","先驅；開創","The firm pioneered online banking in Asia.","這家公司在亞洲開創了網路銀行。"],["revolutionize","/ˌrevəˈluːʃənaɪz/","v.","徹底改革","Smartphones revolutionized the way we work.","智慧型手機徹底改變了我們的工作方式。"],["emerging technology","/ɪˌmɜːrdʒɪŋ tekˈnɑːlədʒi/","phr.","新興科技","The conference focuses on emerging technologies.","這場研討會聚焦於新興科技。"],["start-up","/ˈstɑːrt ʌp/","n.","新創公司","She left her job to join a tech start-up.","她辭職加入一家科技新創公司。"],["deadlock","/ˈdedlɑːk/","n.","僵局","The talks ended in deadlock.","談判陷入僵局。"],["validity","/vəˈlɪdəti/","n.","有效性；效期","The validity of the offer is thirty days.","這份報價的有效期限為三十天。"],["infringement","/ɪnˈfrɪndʒmənt/","n.","侵權、違反","The company was sued for patent infringement.","該公司因專利侵權被告。"],["governance","/ˈɡʌvərnəns/","n.","治理、管理","The board is responsible for good governance.","董事會負責確保良好的治理。"],["prohibition","/ˌproʊəˈbɪʃən/","n.","禁止；禁令","There is a prohibition on smoking in the building.","大樓內禁止吸菸。"],["restrictive","/rɪˈstrɪktɪv/","adj.","限制性的","The new rules are too restrictive for small firms.","新規定對小公司來說限制太多。"],["standardize","/ˈstændərdaɪz/","v.","使標準化","We plan to standardize our contracts.","我們計畫將合約標準化。"],["reorganization","/riˌɔːrɡənəˈzeɪʃən/","n.","改組、重整","After the reorganization, I report to a new manager.","改組後我向新的主管報告。"],["foresee","/fɔːrˈsiː/","v.","預見、預料","We don't foresee any delays.","我們預計不會有任何延誤。"],["buyout","/ˈbaɪaʊt/","n.","全面收購、買斷","The management buyout was approved by shareholders.","管理層收購案獲股東通過。"],["mediation","/ˌmiːdiˈeɪʃən/","n.","調解","The case was settled through mediation.","此案透過調解解決。"],["damages","/ˈdæmɪdʒɪz/","n.","損害賠償金","The court ordered the company to pay damages.","法院判決公司支付損害賠償。"],["revoke","/rɪˈvoʊk/","v.","撤銷、吊銷","The agency revoked the company's license.","主管機關吊銷了該公司的執照。"],["second the motion","/ˌsekənd ðə ˈmoʊʃən/","phr.","附議","Ms. Wang seconded the motion to raise prices.","王女士附議漲價的動議。"],["deliberation","/dɪˌlɪbəˈreɪʃən/","n.","商議、審議；深思熟慮","After much deliberation, the board chose a new CEO.","經過多番商議，董事會選出了新執行長。"],["debrief","/ˌdiːˈbriːf/","v.","聽取（任務後）匯報","The manager debriefed the team after the trade show.","商展結束後經理聽取了團隊的匯報。"],["underline","/ˌʌndərˈlaɪn/","v.","強調；在…下畫線","The report underlines the need for new rules.","報告強調了制定新規定的必要性。"],["eloquent","/ˈeləkwənt/","adj.","口才好的、雄辯的","She gave an eloquent speech at the conference.","她在研討會上發表了一場精彩的演說。"],["bargaining power","/ˈbɑːrɡənɪŋ ˌpaʊər/","phr.","議價能力","Large buyers have more bargaining power.","大買家有較強的議價能力。"],["impasse","/ˈɪmpæs/","n.","僵局、死胡同","Negotiations reached an impasse over wages.","談判在薪資問題上陷入僵局。"],["stalemate","/ˈsteɪlmeɪt/","n.","僵持局面","The talks have been in a stalemate for weeks.","談判已僵持了好幾週。"],["mutually","/ˈmjuːtʃuəli/","adv.","相互地、彼此","Let's find a mutually convenient time to meet.","我們找個雙方都方便的時間見面吧。"],["reciprocal","/rɪˈsɪprəkəl/","adj.","互惠的、相互的","The two firms signed a reciprocal agreement.","兩家公司簽署了互惠協議。"],["stipulation","/ˌstɪpjəˈleɪʃən/","n.","（合約的）規定、條款","The loan comes with several stipulations.","這筆貸款附帶數項規定。"],["signatory","/ˈsɪɡnətɔːri/","n.","簽署人、簽約方","All signatories must attend the ceremony.","所有簽約方都必須出席儀式。"],["execute a contract","/ˌeksɪkjuːt ə ˈkɑːntrækt/","phr.","簽署並生效合約","The contract was executed on April 3.","合約已於四月三日正式簽署。"],["bind","/baɪnd/","v.","約束、使受（法律）約束","This agreement binds both parties for five years.","本協議對雙方具五年約束力。"],["null and void","/ˌnʌl ən ˈvɔɪd/","phr.","無效的","The contract was declared null and void.","這份合約被宣告無效。"],["expiry","/ɪkˈspaɪri/","n.","期滿、到期","The lease is due for renewal before its expiry.","租約到期前需要續約。"],["in breach of","/ɪn ˈbriːtʃ əv/","phr.","違反","The supplier is in breach of the agreement.","供應商違反了協議。"],["adherence","/ədˈhɪrəns/","n.","遵守、堅持","Strict adherence to the rules is expected.","公司要求嚴格遵守規定。"],["noncompliance","/ˌnɑːnkəmˈplaɪəns/","n.","違規、不遵守","Noncompliance may result in heavy fines.","違規可能導致高額罰款。"],["conform","/kənˈfɔːrm/","v.","符合、遵從","All products must conform with local laws.","所有產品都必須符合當地法律。"],["obligatory","/əˈblɪɡətɔːri/","adj.","義務的、強制的","Safety training is obligatory for all workers.","所有員工都必須參加安全訓練。"],["oblige","/əˈblaɪdʒ/","v.","迫使、使負有義務","The law obliges companies to publish their accounts.","法律規定公司必須公開帳目。"],["indemnity","/ɪnˈdemnəti/","n.","賠償（保證）、補償","The contract includes an indemnity clause.","合約中包含一項賠償條款。"],["sanction","/ˈsæŋkʃən/","n./v.","制裁；批准","Trade sanctions have hurt our exports.","貿易制裁影響了我們的出口。"],["enforcement","/ɪnˈfɔːrsmənt/","n.","執行、實施（法規）","Enforcement of the new rules starts in July.","新規定將於七月開始執行。"],["legislate","/ˈledʒɪsleɪt/","v.","立法","The government plans to legislate on data privacy.","政府計畫針對資料隱私立法。"],["statutory","/ˈstætʃətɔːri/","adj.","法定的","Employees receive statutory holidays.","員工享有法定假日。"],["ordinance","/ˈɔːrdənəns/","n.","條例、法令","A city ordinance limits noise after 10 p.m.","市政條例限制晚上十點後的噪音。"],["bylaw","/ˈbaɪlɔː/","n.","（公司）章程細則；地方法規","The company bylaws require an annual meeting.","公司章程規定每年須召開大會。"],["bribery","/ˈbraɪbəri/","n.","行賄、受賄","Bribery is strictly forbidden by company policy.","公司政策嚴禁行賄受賄。"],["allegation","/ˌæləˈɡeɪʃən/","n.","（未經證實的）指控","The company denies all allegations of fraud.","公司否認所有詐欺指控。"],["allege","/əˈledʒ/","v.","聲稱、指控","The lawsuit alleges that the product is unsafe.","訴訟中聲稱該產品不安全。"],["testify","/ˈtestɪfaɪ/","v.","作證","The manager was asked to testify in court.","那位經理被傳喚出庭作證。"],["testimony","/ˈtestəmoʊni/","n.","證詞、證言","His testimony helped the company win the case.","他的證詞幫公司打贏了官司。"],["counsel","/ˈkaʊnsəl/","n./v.","律師、法律顧問；建議","The company's counsel reviewed the agreement.","公司的法律顧問審閱了這份協議。"],["legal action","/ˌliːɡəl ˈækʃən/","phr.","法律行動、訴訟","The client threatened legal action over the delay.","客戶揚言要對延誤提起訴訟。"],["waiver","/ˈweɪvər/","n.","棄權聲明；免除","Participants must sign a waiver before the event.","參加者活動前必須簽署棄權聲明。"],["privilege","/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ/","n.","特權、優待","Members enjoy special privileges.","會員享有特別優待。"],["patented","/ˈpætəntɪd/","adj.","取得專利的","Our machine uses patented technology.","我們的機器使用專利技術。"],["licensee","/ˌlaɪsənˈsiː/","n.","被授權人、執照持有人","The licensee must pay royalties each quarter.","被授權方每季都必須支付權利金。"],["classified","/ˈklæsɪfaɪd/","adj.","機密的","These documents are classified.","這些文件屬於機密。"],["governing","/ˈɡʌvərnɪŋ/","adj.","管理的、支配的","The contract states the governing law is Taiwanese law.","合約載明準據法為台灣法律。"],["corporate governance","/ˌkɔːrpərət ˈɡʌvərnəns/","phr.","公司治理","Investors care about strong corporate governance.","投資人重視健全的公司治理。"],["deregulation","/diːˌreɡjəˈleɪʃən/","n.","解除管制、鬆綁","Deregulation opened the market to new companies.","管制鬆綁讓新公司得以進入市場。"],["regulatory body","/ˈreɡjələtɔːri ˌbɑːdi/","phr.","監管機構","A regulatory body oversees the banking sector.","一個監管機構負責監督銀行業。"],["overturn","/ˌoʊvərˈtɝːn/","v.","推翻、撤銷（決定）","The court overturned the earlier ruling.","法院推翻了先前的判決。"],["repeal","/rɪˈpiːl/","v./n.","廢除（法律）","Lawmakers voted to repeal the old tax.","立法者投票廢除了舊稅。"],["policymaker","/ˈpɑːləsiˌmeɪkər/","n.","決策者、政策制定者","Policymakers are discussing new trade rules.","政策制定者正在討論新的貿易規則。"],["directive","/dəˈrektɪv/","n.","指令、指示","Staff received a directive to reduce travel.","員工收到減少出差的指令。"],["core competence","/ˌkɔːr ˈkɑːmpətəns/","phr.","核心能力","Precision engineering is our core competence.","精密工程是我們的核心能力。"],["consolidation","/kənˌsɑːləˈdeɪʃən/","n.","合併、整併；鞏固","Consolidation in the industry has reduced competition.","產業整併使競爭減少了。"],["spin off","/ˌspɪn ˈɔːf/","phr.","分拆（部門成立新公司）","The firm plans to spin off its software unit.","這家公司計畫分拆其軟體部門。"],["countermeasure","/ˈkaʊntərˌmeʒər/","n.","對策、反制措施","We discussed countermeasures against price cuts.","我們討論了因應降價的對策。"],["discretion","/dɪˈskreʃən/","n.","斟酌權、自行決定；謹慎","Bonuses are paid at the manager's discretion.","獎金由經理斟酌發放。"],["at one's discretion","/æt wʌnz dɪˈskreʃən/","phr.","由某人自行決定","Refunds are given at the store's discretion.","是否退款由店家自行決定。"],["empowerment","/ɪmˈpaʊərmənt/","n.","授權、賦權","Employee empowerment improves job satisfaction.","賦權員工能提升工作滿意度。"],["accountable to","/əˈkaʊntəbəl tuː/","phr.","對…負責","Managers are accountable to the shareholders.","經理人要對股東負責。"],["affiliated","/əˈfɪlieɪtɪd/","adj.","附屬的、有關聯的","The hotel is affiliated with a global chain.","這家飯店隸屬於一家國際連鎖集團。"],["acquirer","/əˈkwaɪərər/","n.","收購方","The acquirer agreed to keep all employees.","收購方同意留任所有員工。"],["hostile takeover","/ˌhɑːstəl ˈteɪkoʊvər/","phr.","惡意收購","The board rejected the hostile takeover bid.","董事會拒絕了惡意收購的出價。"],["buy out","/ˌbaɪ ˈaʊt/","phr.","買下（全部股份）","She bought out her partner's share of the business.","她買下了合夥人在公司的股份。"],["bidder","/ˈbɪdər/","n.","投標者、出價者","The contract went to the lowest bidder.","合約給了出價最低的投標者。"],["tender offer","/ˈtendər ˌɔːfər/","phr.","公開收購要約","The firm made a tender offer for its rival's shares.","該公司對競爭對手的股票提出公開收購。"],["joint","/dʒɔɪnt/","adj.","共同的、聯合的","The two firms issued a joint statement.","兩家公司發表了聯合聲明。"],["ally","/ˈælaɪ/","n./v.","盟友；結盟","The company is a key ally in our expansion.","這家公司是我們擴張的重要盟友。"],["strategic alliance","/strəˌtiːdʒɪk əˈlaɪəns/","phr.","策略聯盟","We formed a strategic alliance with a Korean firm.","我們和一家韓國公司結成策略聯盟。"],["subcontract","/ˌsʌbkənˈtrækt/","v.","轉包、分包","We subcontract the electrical work to a local firm.","我們把電氣工程分包給當地公司。"],["outsource to","/ˈaʊtsɔːrs tuː/","phr.","外包給","We outsource customer support to an agency.","我們把客服外包給一家代理商。"],["franchisee","/ˌfræntʃaɪˈziː/","n.","加盟店主、加盟業者","Each franchisee pays a monthly fee.","每位加盟業者每月支付費用。"],["memorandum of understanding","/ˌmeməˌrændəm əv ˌʌndərˈstændɪŋ/","phr.","合作備忘錄（MOU）","The two companies signed a memorandum of understanding.","兩家公司簽署了合作備忘錄。"],["letter of intent","/ˌletər əv ɪnˈtent/","phr.","意向書","The buyer sent a letter of intent last week.","買方上週寄來了意向書。"],["undertaking","/ˌʌndərˈteɪkɪŋ/","n.","（艱鉅的）任務、事業；承諾","Building a new plant is a major undertaking.","興建新工廠是一項重大任務。"],["commencement","/kəˈmensmənt/","n.","開始、開工","Payment is due on commencement of work.","款項於開工時支付。"],["resources","/ˈriːsɔːrsɪz/","n.","資源（人力、物力）","We lack the resources to finish on time.","我們缺乏如期完成的資源。"],["subcommittee","/ˈsʌbkəˌmɪti/","n.","小組委員會","A subcommittee will review the budget.","將由小組委員會審查預算。"],["viability","/ˌvaɪəˈbɪləti/","n.","可行性、生存能力","We are studying the viability of the project.","我們正在研究這個專案的可行性。"],["renegotiation","/ˌriːnɪˌɡoʊʃiˈeɪʃən/","n.","重新協商","The renegotiation of the lease took months.","重新協商租約花了好幾個月。"],["term sheet","/ˈtɝːm ˌʃiːt/","phr.","投資條件書","The investors sent us a term sheet.","投資人寄給我們一份投資條件書。"],["ratification","/ˌrætəfəˈkeɪʃən/","n.","批准、正式認可","The agreement awaits ratification by the board.","該協議尚待董事會批准。"],["sanctioned","/ˈsæŋkʃənd/","adj.","經批准的；受制裁的","Only sanctioned events may use the company name.","只有經核准的活動才能使用公司名稱。"],["object","/əbˈdʒekt/","v.","反對、提出異議","Several shareholders objected strongly.","幾位股東強烈反對。"],["arbitrate","/ˈɑːrbətreɪt/","v.","仲裁","An expert was hired to arbitrate the dispute.","請了一位專家來仲裁這起爭議。"],["dissolve","/dɪˈzɑːlv/","v.","解散；終止（合夥）","The partners agreed to dissolve the business.","合夥人同意解散公司。"],["dissolution","/ˌdɪsəˈluːʃən/","n.","解散、終止","The dissolution of the partnership was friendly.","合夥關係和平解散。"],["annul","/əˈnʌl/","v.","宣告無效、取消","The court annulled the agreement.","法院宣告該協議無效。"],["fixed-term","/ˌfɪkst ˈtɝːm/","adj.","有固定期限的","She was hired on a fixed-term contract.","她以定期合約受僱。"],["open-ended","/ˌoʊpən ˈendɪd/","adj.","無限期的；開放式的","The agreement is open-ended with no end date.","這份協議沒有截止日，屬無限期。"],["escape clause","/ɪˈskeɪp ˌklɔːz/","phr.","免責條款、退出條款","The contract has an escape clause for emergencies.","合約中有針對緊急狀況的退出條款。"],["exclusivity","/ˌekskluːˈsɪvəti/","n.","獨家性、排他性","The deal gives us exclusivity for three years.","這筆交易給我們三年的獨家權。"],["non-compete","/ˌnɑːn kəmˈpiːt/","adj.","競業禁止的","He signed a non-compete agreement when he joined.","他入職時簽了競業禁止協議。"],["full disclosure","/ˌfʊl dɪsˈkloʊʒər/","phr.","完全揭露、全盤公開","In the interest of full disclosure, I own shares in the firm.","為了完全揭露，我持有該公司的股份。"],["acknowledgment","/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒmənt/","n.","確認（收到）；承認","Please send an acknowledgment of the order.","請寄送訂單確認回函。"],["sign-off","/ˈsaɪn ɔːf/","n.","批准、簽核","We need the client's sign-off before printing.","印刷前需要客戶簽核。"],["undersigned","/ˌʌndərˈsaɪnd/","n.","簽署人、文末簽名者","We, the undersigned, agree to these terms.","我們，以下簽名者，同意上述條款。"],["regulatory compliance","/ˌreɡjələtɔːri kəmˈplaɪəns/","phr.","法規遵循","Regulatory compliance is costly for small banks.","法規遵循對小型銀行來說成本很高。"],["point of order","/ˌpɔɪnt əv ˈɔːrdər/","phr.","議事程序問題","He raised a point of order during the debate.","他在辯論中提出了程序問題。"],["preliminary agreement","/prɪˌlɪmɪneri əˈɡriːmənt/","phr.","初步協議","The firms reached a preliminary agreement on price.","兩家公司在價格上達成初步協議。"],["binding offer","/ˌbaɪndɪŋ ˈɔːfər/","phr.","具約束力的要約","The buyer has not yet made a binding offer.","買方尚未提出具約束力的要約。"],["fiduciary duty","/fɪˈduːʃieri ˌduːti/","phr.","受託義務","Directors have a fiduciary duty to shareholders.","董事對股東負有受託義務。"],["on the condition that","/ɑːn ðə kənˈdɪʃən ðæt/","conj.","在……條件下","You can use the car on the condition that you pay for gas.","你可以用車，條件是你付油錢。"],["in the event that","/ɪn ði ɪˈvɛnt ðæt/","conj.","萬一、倘若","In the event that you are late, call us.","萬一您會遲到，請來電告知。"],["lead up to","/ˌliːd ˈʌp tə/","phr.","在……之前的一段時間","Sales rise in the weeks leading up to the holidays.","假期前幾週銷售額會上升。"],["hold off","/ˌhoʊld ˈɔːf/","phr.","延緩、暫緩","Let's hold off on hiring until next year.","我們暫緩招聘到明年吧。"],["be in a position to","/bi ɪn ə pəˈzɪʃən tə/","phr.","能夠、有條件做","We are not in a position to lower the price.","我們無法再降價。"],["be comparable to","/bi ˈkɑːmpərəbəl tə/","phr.","可與……相比","Our quality is comparable to the leading brands.","我們的品質可媲美領先品牌。"],["be engaged in","/bi ɪnˈɡeɪdʒd ɪn/","phr.","從事、忙於","The company is engaged in software development.","這家公司從事軟體開發。"],["provided that","/prəˈvaɪdɪd ðæt/","conj.","只要、倘若","You may leave early provided that your work is done.","只要工作完成，你就可以提早離開。"],["providing that","/prəˈvaɪdɪŋ ðæt/","conj.","只要、倘若","We'll sign providing that the terms are acceptable.","只要條款可以接受，我們就簽約。"],["given that","/ˈɡɪvən ðæt/","conj.","考慮到、鑑於","Given that sales are down, we must cut costs.","鑑於銷售下滑，我們必須削減成本。"],["assuming that","/əˈsuːmɪŋ ðæt/","conj.","假設","Assuming that the parts arrive, we'll finish Friday.","假設零件到貨，我們週五可以完成。"],["seeing that","/ˈsiːɪŋ ðæt/","conj.","既然、由於","Seeing that everyone is here, let's begin.","既然大家都到了，我們開始吧。"],["in that","/ɪn ˈðæt/","conj.","因為、在於","The plan is risky in that it requires a large loan.","這計畫有風險，因為需要大筆貸款。"],["so as to","/ˈsoʊ æz tə/","phr.","為了","We extended hours so as to serve more customers.","我們延長營業時間以服務更多客戶。"],["thus","/ðʌs/","adv.","因此；如此","Costs fell, thus improving our margins.","成本下降，因而提高了利潤率。"],["furthermore","/ˈfɜːrðərmɔːr/","adv.","此外、再者","Furthermore, all staff must attend the training.","此外，所有員工都必須參加訓練。"],["nonetheless","/ˌnʌnðəˈlɛs/","adv.","儘管如此","The test failed; nonetheless, we learned a lot.","測試失敗了，儘管如此我們學到很多。"],["otherwise","/ˈʌðərwaɪz/","adv.","否則；在其他方面","Please pay by Friday; otherwise, a fee will apply.","請於週五前付款，否則將收取費用。"],["meanwhile","/ˈmiːnwaɪl/","adv.","同時、在此期間","Meanwhile, the IT team will update the system.","同時，資訊團隊會更新系統。"],["likewise","/ˈlaɪkwaɪz/","adv.","同樣地","The managers agreed, and likewise the staff.","經理們同意了，員工也同樣同意。"],["conversely","/kənˈvɜːrsli/","adv.","相反地","Conversely, smaller firms reported higher profits.","相反地，小型公司的利潤較高。"],["alternatively","/ɔːlˈtɜːrnətɪvli/","adv.","或者、另外","Alternatively, you can pay at the front desk.","或者，您也可以在櫃台付款。"],["previously","/ˈpriːviəsli/","adv.","先前","As previously mentioned, the office will move.","如先前所述，辦公室將搬遷。"],["respectively","/rɪˈspɛktɪvli/","adv.","分別地","Sales in May and June were 3 and 4 million, respectively.","五月和六月的銷售額分別為三百萬和四百萬。"],["sharply","/ˈʃɑːrpli/","adv.","急遽地","Profits dropped sharply in the third quarter.","第三季獲利急遽下滑。"],["readily","/ˈrɛdɪli/","adv.","容易地；樂意地","Spare parts are readily available.","備用零件很容易取得。"],["thoroughly","/ˈθɜːroʊli/","adv.","徹底地","Please read the contract thoroughly.","請仔細閱讀合約。"],["accurately","/ˈækjərətli/","adv.","準確地","Fill out the form accurately.","請準確填寫表格。"],["regardless of","/rɪˈɡɑːrdləs əv/","prep.","不論","Regardless of the weather, the event will go on.","不論天氣如何，活動都會照常舉行。"],["in compliance with the law","/ɪn kəmˈplaɪəns wɪð ðə ˈlɔː/","phr.","依法、遵守法律","The plant operates in compliance with the law.","工廠依法運作。"],["in accordance with the terms","/ɪn əˈkɔːrdəns wɪð ðə ˈtɜːrmz/","phr.","依照條款","Payment will be made in accordance with the terms.","將依照條款付款。"],["in recognition of","/ɪn ˌrɛkəɡˈnɪʃən əv/","phr.","為表彰","She received an award in recognition of her service.","她因服務表現獲頒獎項以示表彰。"],["in appreciation of","/ɪn əˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃən əv/","phr.","為感謝","In appreciation of your loyalty, here is a gift card.","為感謝您的支持，贈送禮物卡一張。"],["in celebration of","/ɪn ˌsɛləˈbreɪʃən əv/","phr.","為慶祝","A dinner was held in celebration of our anniversary.","為慶祝週年舉辦了晚宴。"],["in honor of","/ɪn ˈɑːnər əv/","phr.","為紀念、向……致敬","The party is in honor of the retiring director.","這場派對是為即將退休的主任舉辦的。"],["in return for","/ɪn rɪˈtɜːrn fɔːr/","phr.","作為回報","In return for a deposit, we'll hold the room.","支付訂金後，我們會為您保留房間。"],["in preparation for","/ɪn ˌprɛpəˈreɪʃən fɔːr/","phr.","為……做準備","Staff cleaned the lobby in preparation for the visit.","員工打掃大廳，為來訪做準備。"],["in anticipation of","/ɪn ænˌtɪsɪˈpeɪʃən əv/","phr.","預期、以待","We hired more staff in anticipation of the holidays.","我們預期假期旺季而增聘人手。"],["in pursuit of","/ɪn pərˈsuːt əv/","phr.","追求","The company is in pursuit of new markets.","公司正在開拓新市場。"],["in the absence of","/ɪn ði ˈæbsəns əv/","phr.","在缺乏……的情況下；……不在時","In the absence of the manager, Ann will decide.","經理不在時由 Ann 決定。"],["in the presence of","/ɪn ðə ˈprɛzəns əv/","phr.","在……面前","The contract was signed in the presence of a lawyer.","合約在律師見證下簽署。"],["in the wake of","/ɪn ðə ˈweɪk əv/","phr.","在……之後、緊接著","In the wake of the merger, many jobs were cut.","合併之後，許多職位被裁撤。"],["in the interest of","/ɪn ði ˈɪntrəst əv/","phr.","為了……的利益","In the interest of safety, the area is closed.","為了安全，該區域已封閉。"],["in excess of","/ɪn ˈɛksɛs əv/","phr.","超過","Orders in excess of 100 units get a discount.","訂單超過 100 件可享折扣。"],["in keeping with","/ɪn ˈkiːpɪŋ wɪð/","phr.","與……一致","In keeping with tradition, we close on New Year's Day.","依照慣例，我們元旦公休。"],["in the vicinity of","/ɪn ðə vəˈsɪnəti əv/","phr.","在……附近；大約","There are several hotels in the vicinity of the airport.","機場附近有幾家飯店。"],["in proportion to","/ɪn prəˈpɔːrʃən tə/","phr.","與……成比例","Bonuses are paid in proportion to sales.","獎金依銷售額比例發放。"],["in contrast to","/ɪn ˈkɑːntræst tə/","phr.","與……相比、相對於","In contrast to last year, sales are up.","與去年相比，銷售額成長了。"],["in the course of","/ɪn ðə ˈkɔːrs əv/","phr.","在……過程中","In the course of the audit, errors were found.","審計過程中發現了錯誤。"],["in the face of","/ɪn ðə ˈfeɪs əv/","phr.","面對","The firm grew in the face of strong competition.","面對激烈競爭，公司仍持續成長。"],["in accordance with company policy","/ɪn əˈkɔːrdəns wɪð ˈkʌmpəni ˈpɑːləsi/","phr.","依照公司政策","Refunds are issued in accordance with company policy.","退款依公司政策辦理。"],["on behalf of the company","/ɑːn bɪˈhæf əv ðə ˈkʌmpəni/","phr.","代表公司","I'd like to thank you on behalf of the company.","我謹代表公司向您致謝。"],["on the premises","/ɑːn ðə ˈprɛmɪsɪz/","phr.","在建築物內、在場所內","Smoking is not allowed on the premises.","本場所內禁止吸菸。"],["on a trial basis","/ɑːn ə ˈtraɪəl ˈbeɪsɪs/","phr.","試行地","The new schedule will run on a trial basis.","新班表將先試行。"],["on a case-by-case basis","/ɑːn ə ˌkeɪs baɪ ˈkeɪs ˈbeɪsɪs/","phr.","個案處理","Refund requests are reviewed on a case-by-case basis.","退款申請採個案審核。"],["on the verge of","/ɑːn ðə ˈvɜːrdʒ əv/","phr.","瀕臨、即將","The two firms are on the verge of a deal.","兩家公司即將達成協議。"],["on the rise","/ɑːn ðə ˈraɪz/","phr.","上升中","Online orders are on the rise.","線上訂單正在增加。"],["on the decline","/ɑːn ðə dɪˈklaɪn/","phr.","下降中","Print advertising is on the decline.","平面廣告正在衰退。"],["on file","/ɑːn ˈfaɪl/","phr.","存檔備查","We will keep your résumé on file.","我們會將您的履歷存檔。"],["on loan","/ɑːn ˈloʊn/","phr.","借出中","The painting is on loan from a museum.","這幅畫是向博物館借展的。"],["on the agenda","/ɑːn ði əˈdʒɛndə/","phr.","列入議程","What's the first item on the agenda?","議程的第一項是什麼？"],["on a weekly basis","/ɑːn ə ˈwiːkli ˈbeɪsɪs/","phr.","每週","Reports are submitted on a weekly basis.","報告每週提交一次。"],["at the discretion of the manager","/æt ðə dɪˈskrɛʃən əv ðə ˈmænɪdʒər/","phr.","由經理斟酌決定","Overtime is approved at the discretion of the manager.","加班由經理斟酌核准。"],["at one's convenience","/æt wʌnz kənˈviːniəns/","phr.","在某人方便時","Please call me back at your convenience.","請在您方便時回電給我。"],["at the cost of","/æt ðə ˈkɔːst əv/","phr.","以……為代價","They met the deadline at the cost of quality.","他們以犧牲品質為代價趕上期限。"],["at the forefront of","/æt ðə ˈfɔːrfrʌnt əv/","phr.","在……的最前線","The firm is at the forefront of solar technology.","該公司走在太陽能技術的最前線。"],["at the outset","/æt ði ˈaʊtsɛt/","phr.","一開始","We set clear goals at the outset.","我們一開始就設定了明確目標。"],["at the earliest","/æt ði ˈɜːrliɪst/","phr.","最早","The parts will arrive Monday at the earliest.","零件最早週一到貨。"],["at full capacity","/æt ˈfʊl kəˈpæsəti/","phr.","滿載、全力運轉","The factory is running at full capacity.","工廠正全力運轉。"],["at a loss","/æt ə ˈlɔːs/","phr.","虧本地；不知所措","The shop sold the old stock at a loss.","商店虧本出清舊庫存。"],["at random","/æt ˈrændəm/","phr.","隨機地","Ten customers were chosen at random.","隨機選出了十位顧客。"],["at stake","/æt ˈsteɪk/","phr.","有風險、攸關","A major contract is at stake.","一份大合約岌岌可危。"],["at odds with","/æt ˈɑːdz wɪð/","phr.","與……不一致、不和","The figures are at odds with last month's report.","這些數字與上個月的報告不符。"],["at the latest by","/æt ðə ˈleɪtɪst baɪ/","phr.","最遲在……之前","Please reply at the latest by Friday noon.","請最晚於週五中午前回覆。"],["by way of","/baɪ ˈweɪ əv/","prep.","經由；作為","We flew to Paris by way of Dubai.","我們經杜拜飛往巴黎。"],["by the same token","/baɪ ðə ˈseɪm ˈtoʊkən/","phr.","同樣地","By the same token, costs should also fall.","同樣地，成本也應該會下降。"],["by popular demand","/baɪ ˈpɑːpjələr dɪˈmænd/","phr.","應大眾要求","By popular demand, the show has been extended.","應觀眾要求，演出已延長。"],["for the purpose of","/fɔːr ðə ˈpɜːrpəs əv/","phr.","為了……目的","Data is collected for the purpose of research.","收集資料是為了研究目的。"],["for the sake of","/fɔːr ðə ˈseɪk əv/","phr.","為了","For the sake of time, let's skip the details.","為了節省時間，我們跳過細節吧。"],["for the duration of","/fɔːr ðə djʊˈreɪʃən əv/","phr.","在……整段期間","The road is closed for the duration of the festival.","節慶期間道路封閉。"],["for a fee","/fɔːr ə ˈfiː/","phr.","需付費","Extra luggage can be checked for a fee.","額外行李可付費託運。"],["from now on","/frʌm ˌnaʊ ˈɑːn/","phr.","從現在起","From now on, all expenses need receipts.","從現在起，所有支出都需要收據。"],["from time to time","/frʌm ˈtaɪm tə ˈtaɪm/","phr.","有時、偶爾","We review our prices from time to time.","我們不時會檢討價格。"],["under review","/ˌʌndər rɪˈvjuː/","phr.","審查中","Your application is currently under review.","您的申請目前正在審查中。"],["under way","/ˌʌndər ˈweɪ/","phr.","進行中","Renovations are already under way.","整修工程已經在進行中。"],["under the supervision of","/ˌʌndər ðə ˌsuːpərˈvɪʒən əv/","phr.","在……的監督下","Interns work under the supervision of a manager.","實習生在經理的督導下工作。"],["under the direction of","/ˌʌndər ðə dəˈrɛkʃən əv/","phr.","在……指導下","The project is under the direction of Dr. Wu.","此專案由吳博士指導。"],["under new management","/ˌʌndər ˌnuː ˈmænɪdʒmənt/","phr.","由新團隊經營","The restaurant is now under new management.","這家餐廳現在由新團隊經營。"],["under no circumstances","/ˌʌndər ˈnoʊ ˈsɜːrkəmstænsɪz/","phr.","絕不、在任何情況下都不","Under no circumstances should you share your password.","在任何情況下都不可分享密碼。"],["beyond repair","/bɪˌjɑːnd rɪˈpɛr/","phr.","無法修復","The old copier is beyond repair.","舊影印機已經無法修復。"],["beyond one's control","/bɪˌjɑːnd wʌnz kənˈtroʊl/","phr.","非某人所能控制","The delay was due to circumstances beyond our control.","延誤是由於我們無法控制的情況。"],["with the exception of","/wɪð ði ɪkˈsɛpʃən əv/","phr.","除了……之外","All stores, with the exception of one, are open.","除了一家之外，所有分店都營業。"],["with the aim of","/wɪð ði ˈeɪm əv/","phr.","目的在於","The program was created with the aim of training leaders.","這個計畫的目的在於培養領導者。"],["with reference to","/wɪð ˈrɛfərəns tə/","phr.","關於","With reference to your letter, we accept your offer.","關於您的來信，我們接受您的提議。"],["with the help of","/wɪð ðə ˈhɛlp əv/","phr.","在……的幫助下","We finished the move with the help of volunteers.","在志工協助下我們完成了搬遷。"],["without notice","/wɪˈðaʊt ˈnoʊtɪs/","phr.","未經通知","Schedules may change without notice.","行程可能未經通知而變動。"],["without delay","/wɪˈðaʊt dɪˈleɪ/","phr.","立即、毫不延遲","Please report any damage without delay.","如有任何損壞請立即回報。"],["without exception","/wɪˈðaʊt ɪkˈsɛpʃən/","phr.","毫無例外","All visitors must register without exception.","所有訪客都必須登記，無一例外。"],["ahead of","/əˈhɛd əv/","prep.","在……之前；領先","We finished the project ahead of the deadline.","我們在期限前完成了專案。"],["prior to departure","/ˈpraɪər tə dɪˈpɑːrtʃər/","phr.","出發前","Check in online 24 hours prior to departure.","請於出發前 24 小時線上報到。"],["contrary to","/ˈkɑːntrɛri tə/","prep.","與……相反","Contrary to expectations, sales increased.","與預期相反，銷售額增加了。"],["according to plan","/əˈkɔːrdɪŋ tə ˈplæn/","phr.","按照計畫","The launch went according to plan.","產品發表按照計畫進行。"],["as opposed to","/æz əˈpoʊzd tə/","phr.","而非、與……相對","We prefer email as opposed to phone calls.","我們偏好電子郵件，而非電話。"],["as a consequence","/æz ə ˈkɑːnsəkwəns/","phr.","因此、結果","As a consequence, the event was postponed.","因此，活動延期了。"],["as a rule","/æz ə ˈruːl/","phr.","通常、一般而言","As a rule, we reply within a day.","我們通常一天內回覆。"],["as far as","/æz ˈfɑːr æz/","phr.","就……而言；遠至","As far as I know, the meeting is still on.","據我所知，會議仍照常舉行。"],["as indicated","/æz ˈɪndɪkeɪtɪd/","phr.","如所示","Please sign as indicated on page two.","請依第二頁所示簽名。"],["as stated above","/æz ˈsteɪtɪd əˈbʌv/","phr.","如上所述","As stated above, fees are non-refundable.","如上所述，費用恕不退還。"],["as outlined","/æz ˈaʊtlaɪnd/","phr.","如所概述","As outlined in the memo, hours will change.","如備忘錄所述，工作時間將有所變動。"],["so long as","/soʊ ˈlɔːŋ æz/","conj.","只要","So long as the budget allows, we'll hire two more.","只要預算允許，我們會再招兩人。"],["only if","/ˈoʊnli ɪf/","conj.","只有在……的情況下","Refunds are given only if receipts are provided.","只有提供收據才能退款。"],["if necessary","/ɪf ˈnɛsəsɛri/","phr.","如有必要","We can extend the deadline if necessary.","如有必要，我們可以延長期限。"],["if possible","/ɪf ˈpɑːsəbəl/","phr.","如果可能的話","Please arrive early, if possible.","如果可以的話，請提早抵達。"],["if any","/ɪf ˈɛni/","phr.","如果有的話","Please list your allergies, if any.","如有過敏請列出。"],["unless otherwise noted","/ənˈlɛs ˈʌðərwaɪz ˈnoʊtɪd/","phr.","除非另有註明","Unless otherwise noted, prices include tax.","除非另有註明，價格均含稅。"],["except when","/ɪkˈsɛpt wɛn/","conj.","除了……的時候","The office is open daily except when it's a holiday.","除國定假日外，辦公室每天開放。"],["once","/wʌns/","conj.","一旦","Once the form is approved, you will be notified.","表格一經核准，您將會收到通知。"],["whenever","/wɛnˈɛvər/","conj.","每當；無論何時","Call me whenever you need help.","需要幫忙時隨時打給我。"],["wherever","/wɛrˈɛvər/","conj.","無論何處","Our app works wherever you travel.","無論您到哪裡旅行，我們的應用程式都能使用。"],["whichever","/wɪtʃˈɛvər/","pron./adj.","無論哪一個","Choose whichever plan suits you best.","請選擇最適合您的方案。"],["whoever","/huːˈɛvər/","pron.","無論誰；任何……的人","Whoever finishes first can leave early.","誰先做完就可以先走。"],["whatever","/wʌtˈɛvər/","pron./adj.","無論什麼","We'll do whatever it takes to satisfy clients.","我們會不惜一切讓客戶滿意。"],["concerning","/kənˈsɜːrnɪŋ/","prep.","關於","Do you have questions concerning the contract?","您對合約有任何疑問嗎？"],["beyond","/bɪˈjɑːnd/","prep.","超出；在……之外","The project went beyond its original budget.","專案超出了原本的預算。"],["upon","/əˈpɑːn/","prep.","在……之後立即；一……就","Payment is due upon receipt of the invoice.","收到發票後應立即付款。"],["via","/ˈvaɪə/","prep.","經由、透過","The documents were sent via email.","文件是透過電子郵件寄送的。"],["per","/pɜːr/","prep.","每；依照","The fee is 20 dollars per person.","費用為每人 20 美元。"],["excluding","/ɪkˈskluːdɪŋ/","prep.","不包括","The price is 300 dollars, excluding tax.","價格為 300 美元，不含稅。"],["including","/ɪnˈkluːdɪŋ/","prep.","包括","The package costs 900 dollars, including meals.","套裝行程 900 美元，含餐點。"],["considering","/kənˈsɪdərɪŋ/","prep./conj.","考慮到","Considering the cost, the results are impressive.","考慮到成本，成果令人驚豔。"],["barring","/ˈbɑːrɪŋ/","prep.","除非、若無","Barring delays, the order will arrive Monday.","若無延誤，訂單將於週一到貨。"],["amid","/əˈmɪd/","prep.","在……之中","Stocks fell amid concerns about inflation.","在通膨疑慮中股市下跌。"],["unlike","/ʌnˈlaɪk/","prep.","不像、與……不同","Unlike other banks, we charge no fees.","與其他銀行不同，我們不收手續費。"],["alike","/əˈlaɪk/","adv./adj.","同樣地；相似的","The event appeals to adults and children alike.","這項活動大人小孩都喜歡。"],["albeit","/ɔːlˈbiːɪt/","conj.","雖然、儘管","Sales improved, albeit slowly.","銷售有所改善，雖然速度緩慢。"],["lest","/lɛst/","conj.","以免","Save your work often lest you lose data.","請經常存檔以免遺失資料。"],["hygienist","/haɪˈdʒiːnɪst/","n.","牙科衛生師","The hygienist will clean your teeth first.","牙科衛生師會先幫您洗牙。"],["dental cleaning","/ˌdentl ˈkliːnɪŋ/","phr.","洗牙","Most plans cover two dental cleanings a year.","大多數方案每年給付兩次洗牙。"],["hospitalize","/ˈhɑːspɪtəlaɪz/","v.","使住院","He was hospitalized for three days last month.","他上個月住院了三天。"],["contagious","/kənˈteɪdʒəs/","adj.","傳染性的","Please stay home if your illness is contagious.","如果您的疾病具傳染性，請待在家裡。"],["chronic","/ˈkrɑːnɪk/","adj.","慢性的；長期的","The clinic specializes in chronic pain treatment.","這間診所專門治療慢性疼痛。"],["immune","/ɪˈmjuːn/","adj.","免疫的","A healthy diet supports your immune system.","健康的飲食有助於您的免疫系統。"],["optometrist","/ɑːpˈtɑːmətrɪst/","n.","驗光師","The optometrist recommended new glasses.","驗光師建議配一副新眼鏡。"],["ointment","/ˈɔɪntmənt/","n.","藥膏","Apply the ointment twice a day.","請一天擦兩次藥膏。"],["policyholder","/ˈpɑːləsihoʊldər/","n.","保單持有人、要保人","Policyholders will receive a renewal notice by mail.","保單持有人將會收到郵寄的續保通知。"],["copayment","/ˈkoʊpeɪmənt/","n.","（醫療）部分負擔金額","The copayment for each visit is $20.","每次看診的部分負擔是 20 美元。"],["underwriter","/ˈʌndərraɪtər/","n.","核保人員；承保人","An underwriter will review your application.","核保人員將審核您的申請。"],["walk-in patient","/ˈwɔːk ɪn ˌpeɪʃnt/","phr.","未預約的病患","Walk-in patients may have to wait longer.","未預約的病患可能需要等候較久。"],["periodical","/ˌpɪriˈɑːdɪkl/","n.","期刊","The library subscribes to over 300 periodicals.","圖書館訂閱了超過 300 種期刊。"],["publishing house","/ˈpʌblɪʃɪŋ haʊs/","phr.","出版社","She works as an editor at a publishing house.","她在一家出版社擔任編輯。"],["co-author","/ˈkoʊ ˌɔːθər/","n./v.","共同作者；合著","He co-authored a book on urban planning.","他與人合著了一本關於都市規劃的書。"],["autobiography","/ˌɔːtəbaɪˈɑːɡrəfi/","n.","自傳","The CEO is writing her autobiography.","這位執行長正在寫她的自傳。"],["critique","/krɪˈtiːk/","n./v.","評論；評論、評析","The editor gave a detailed critique of the draft.","編輯對草稿提出了詳細的評析。"],["critically acclaimed","/ˌkrɪtɪkli əˈkleɪmd/","phr.","廣受好評的","The critically acclaimed play returns next month.","這齣廣受好評的舞台劇下個月再度上演。"],["royalty","/ˈrɔɪəlti/","n.","版稅；權利金","Authors receive a royalty on each copy sold.","作者每賣出一本書就能獲得版稅。"],["tabloid","/ˈtæblɔɪd/","n.","小報、八卦報","The story first appeared in a tabloid.","這則消息最早出現在一份八卦小報上。"],["preservation","/ˌprezərˈveɪʃn/","n.","保存、保護","The group works for the preservation of historic buildings.","該團體致力於歷史建築的保存。"],["energy efficiency","/ˈenərdʒi ɪˌfɪʃnsi/","phr.","能源效率","New windows will improve the building's energy efficiency.","新窗戶將提升大樓的能源效率。"],["emissions","/ɪˈmɪʃnz/","n.","排放（量）","The factory has reduced its carbon emissions.","工廠已減少碳排放。"],["solar","/ˈsoʊlər/","adj.","太陽的、太陽能的","The building is partly powered by solar energy.","這棟大樓部分由太陽能供電。"],["biodegradable","/ˌbaɪoʊdɪˈɡreɪdəbl/","adj.","可生物分解的","The cups are made from biodegradable materials.","這些杯子由可生物分解的材料製成。"],["pesticide","/ˈpestɪsaɪd/","n.","殺蟲劑、農藥","The farm grows vegetables without pesticides.","這座農場種植不用農藥的蔬菜。"],["non-profit organization","/ˌnɑːn ˈprɑːfɪt ˌɔːrɡənəˈzeɪʃn/","phr.","非營利組織","The event is run by a non-profit organization.","這項活動由一個非營利組織舉辦。"],["civic","/ˈsɪvɪk/","adj.","市民的、公民的","Volunteering is a good way to show civic pride.","當志工是展現公民榮譽感的好方法。"],["beautification","/bjuːˌtɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","n.","美化","The city launched a street beautification project.","市府推出了一項街道美化計畫。"],["municipal","/mjuːˈnɪsɪpl/","adj.","市政的、市立的","The municipal pool reopens on June 1.","市立游泳池將於六月一日重新開放。"],["council","/ˈkaʊnsl/","n.","議會、委員會","The council discussed the new parking rules.","議會討論了新的停車規定。"],["governmental","/ˌɡʌvərnˈmentl/","adj.","政府的","The project requires governmental approval.","這個計畫需要政府核准。"],["ministry","/ˈmɪnɪstri/","n.","（政府的）部","The Ministry of Health issued new guidelines.","衛生部發布了新的指導方針。"],["federal","/ˈfedərəl/","adj.","聯邦的","The program is supported by federal funds.","這個計畫由聯邦經費支持。"],["legislature","/ˈledʒɪsleɪtʃər/","n.","立法機關","The legislature passed the new tax law.","立法機關通過了新的稅法。"],["hearing","/ˈhɪrɪŋ/","n.","聽證會；聽力","The hearing was postponed until next month.","聽證會延到下個月舉行。"],["ballot","/ˈbælət/","n.","選票；投票","Ballots must be returned by Friday.","選票必須在週五前寄回。"],["elect","/ɪˈlekt/","v.","選舉、選出","She was elected chair of the committee.","她被選為委員會主席。"],["public funds","/ˌpʌblɪk ˈfʌndz/","phr.","公共資金、公款","The park was built using public funds.","這座公園是用公共資金建造的。"],["apply for a permit","/əˌplaɪ fər ə ˈpɜːrmɪt/","phr.","申請許可證","You must apply for a permit to hold a street fair.","舉辦街頭市集必須申請許可證。"],["census","/ˈsensəs/","n.","人口普查","The census is conducted every ten years.","人口普查每十年進行一次。"],["precautionary","/prɪˈkɔːʃəneri/","adj.","預防的、防範的","The road was closed as a precautionary measure.","道路基於預防措施而封閉。"],["marginally","/ˈmɑːrdʒɪnəli/","adv.","略微、少許","Profits rose marginally in the second quarter.","第二季利潤略微上升。"],["comparatively","/kəmˈpærətɪvli/","adv.","比較地、相對地","Rents in this area are comparatively low.","這一區的租金相對較低。"],["virtually","/ˈvɜːrtʃuəli/","adv.","幾乎、實際上；線上地","The new system is virtually error-free.","新系統幾乎沒有錯誤。"],["practically","/ˈpræktɪkli/","adv.","幾乎；實際上","The tickets were practically sold out.","門票幾乎賣光了。"],["partially","/ˈpɑːrʃəli/","adv.","部分地","The road will be partially closed for repairs.","道路將因維修而部分封閉。"],["chiefly","/ˈtʃiːfli/","adv.","主要地","The magazine is aimed chiefly at young readers.","這本雜誌主要針對年輕讀者。"],["solely","/ˈsoʊlli/","adv.","唯一地、僅僅","The program is funded solely by donations.","該計畫完全由捐款資助。"],["merely","/ˈmɪrli/","adv.","僅僅、只不過","This is merely a draft, not the final version.","這只是草稿，不是最終版本。"],["scarcely","/ˈskersli/","adv.","幾乎不；僅僅","There was scarcely enough time to prepare.","幾乎沒有足夠的時間準備。"],["seldom","/ˈseldəm/","adv.","很少、不常","The director seldom gives interviews.","這位總監很少接受採訪。"],["continually","/kənˈtɪnjuəli/","adv.","持續地、一再地","We are continually improving our services.","我們持續改善我們的服務。"],["continuously","/kənˈtɪnjuəsli/","adv.","連續不斷地","The machine has run continuously for 48 hours.","這台機器已連續運轉 48 小時。"],["progressively","/prəˈɡresɪvli/","adv.","逐步地、漸進地","Traffic got progressively worse during the day.","交通狀況在一天中逐漸惡化。"],["swiftly","/ˈswɪftli/","adv.","迅速地","The city acted swiftly to repair the damage.","市府迅速採取行動修復損壞。"],["effectively","/ɪˈfektɪvli/","adv.","有效地；實際上","The new policy effectively reduced waste.","新政策有效減少了浪費。"],["productively","/prəˈdʌktɪvli/","adv.","有成效地","The team worked productively all week.","團隊整週都工作得很有效率。"],["tightly","/ˈtaɪtli/","adv.","緊緊地、嚴密地","Access to the area is tightly controlled.","該區域的出入受到嚴格管制。"],["firmly","/ˈfɜːrmli/","adv.","堅定地；牢固地","The company firmly believes in fair pricing.","公司堅信公平定價。"],["adequately","/ˈædɪkwətli/","adv.","充分地、適當地","Make sure the room is adequately ventilated.","請確保房間通風良好。"],["satisfactorily","/ˌsætɪsˈfæktərəli/","adv.","令人滿意地","The issue was resolved satisfactorily.","問題獲得了圓滿解決。"],["affordably","/əˈfɔːrdəbli/","adv.","價格實惠地","The hotel offers affordably priced rooms.","這家飯店提供價格實惠的房間。"],["courteously","/ˈkɜːrtiəsli/","adv.","有禮貌地、謙恭地","Staff must treat all callers courteously.","員工必須禮貌地對待所有來電者。"],["cordial","/ˈkɔːrdʒəl/","adj.","熱誠的、友好的","We had a cordial meeting with the city officials.","我們與市府官員進行了友好的會談。"],["genuinely","/ˈdʒenjuɪnli/","adv.","真誠地、真正地","We are genuinely sorry for the delay.","我們對延誤深感抱歉。"],["collectively","/kəˈlektɪvli/","adv.","共同地、集體地","The residents collectively decided to plant trees.","居民們共同決定種樹。"],["independently","/ˌɪndɪˈpendəntli/","adv.","獨立地","Each clinic operates independently.","每間診所都獨立營運。"],["indirectly","/ˌɪndəˈrektli/","adv.","間接地","The new law will indirectly affect small firms.","新法將間接影響小型企業。"],["provisional","/prəˈvɪʒənl/","adj.","暫時的、臨時的","The dates are provisional and may change.","這些日期是暫定的，可能會變動。"],["conditionally","/kənˈdɪʃənəli/","adv.","有條件地","The plan was conditionally approved by the council.","該計畫獲議會有條件通過。"],["evidently","/ˈevɪdəntli/","adv.","顯然地","Evidently, the new policy has been effective.","顯然，新政策已經奏效。"],["undoubtedly","/ʌnˈdaʊtɪdli/","adv.","無疑地","This is undoubtedly our best year so far.","這無疑是我們至今最好的一年。"],["presumably","/prɪˈzuːməbli/","adv.","大概、據推測","The package was presumably sent to the wrong address.","包裹大概是寄錯地址了。"],["supposedly","/səˈpoʊzɪdli/","adv.","據稱、據說","The repairs were supposedly finished last week.","據說維修上週就完成了。"],["allegedly","/əˈledʒɪdli/","adv.","據稱","The company allegedly violated safety rules.","該公司據稱違反了安全規定。"],["reportedly","/rɪˈpɔːrtɪdli/","adv.","據報導","The firm is reportedly planning to expand.","據報導該公司正計畫擴張。"],["seemingly","/ˈsiːmɪŋli/","adv.","表面上、看似","The seemingly simple task took all day.","這項看似簡單的任務花了一整天。"],["potentially","/pəˈtenʃəli/","adv.","潛在地、可能地","The storm could potentially delay flights.","暴風雨可能會延誤航班。"],["remarkably","/rɪˈmɑːrkəbli/","adv.","顯著地、非常","The clinic's waiting times are remarkably short.","這間診所的候診時間非常短。"],["notably","/ˈnoʊtəbli/","adv.","顯著地；尤其","Sales rose notably in the Asian market.","亞洲市場的銷售明顯成長。"],["explicitly","/ɪkˈsplɪsɪtli/","adv.","明確地","The contract explicitly states the deadline.","合約中明確寫出截止期限。"],["deliberately","/dɪˈlɪbərətli/","adv.","故意地；審慎地","The price was deliberately kept low.","價格被刻意壓低。"],["intentionally","/ɪnˈtenʃənəli/","adv.","故意地、有意地","No one intentionally deleted the files.","沒有人是故意刪除那些檔案的。"],["accidentally","/ˌæksɪˈdentəli/","adv.","意外地、不小心地","I accidentally sent the e-mail to the wrong client.","我不小心把電子郵件寄給錯的客戶。"],["mistakenly","/mɪˈsteɪkənli/","adv.","錯誤地、誤","The bill was mistakenly sent twice.","帳單被誤寄了兩次。"],["erroneously","/ɪˈroʊniəsli/","adv.","錯誤地","You were erroneously charged a late fee.","您被誤收了一筆滯納金。"],["concurrently","/kənˈkɜːrəntli/","adv.","同時地","The two projects will run concurrently.","這兩個專案將同時進行。"],["until further notice","/ənˌtɪl ˌfɜːrðər ˈnoʊtɪs/","phr.","直到另行通知","The pool is closed until further notice.","游泳池關閉，直到另行通知。"],["subject to change","/ˌsʌbdʒɪkt tə ˈtʃeɪndʒ/","phr.","可能會變動","The schedule is subject to change without notice.","行程可能隨時變動，恕不另行通知。"],["be exposed to","/bi ɪkˈspoʊzd tuː/","phr.","暴露於…；接觸到…","Workers should not be exposed to loud noise.","工人不應暴露在高噪音環境中。"],["be renowned for","/bi rɪˈnaʊnd fɔːr/","phr.","以…著稱","The hospital is renowned for its heart surgery.","這家醫院以心臟手術著稱。"],["be noted for","/bi ˈnoʊtɪd fɔːr/","phr.","以…聞名","The region is noted for its clean air.","這個地區以空氣清新聞名。"],["insufficient","/ˌɪnsəˈfɪʃnt/","adj.","不足的","The application was rejected due to insufficient information.","申請因資料不足而遭駁回。"],["ample","/ˈæmpl/","adj.","充足的、寬敞的","There is ample parking behind the building.","大樓後方有充足的停車位。"],["plentiful","/ˈplentɪfl/","adj.","豐富的、充足的","Jobs are plentiful in the health care sector.","醫療照護產業的工作機會很多。"],["prolonged","/prəˈlɔːŋd/","adj.","長期的、持續很久的","Prolonged exposure to the sun can be harmful.","長時間曝曬在陽光下可能有害。"],["forthcoming","/ˌfɔːrθˈkʌmɪŋ/","adj.","即將到來的；即將出版的","Details will be announced in a forthcoming newsletter.","詳情將在即將發行的電子報中公布。"],["impending","/ɪmˈpendɪŋ/","adj.","即將發生的","Residents were warned of the impending storm.","居民被警告暴風雨即將來襲。"],["supplementary","/ˌsʌplɪˈmentri/","adj.","補充的、額外的","Supplementary materials are available online.","補充資料可在線上取得。"],["eminent","/ˈemɪnənt/","adj.","傑出的、著名的","An eminent scientist will give the keynote speech.","一位傑出的科學家將發表主題演講。"],["distinguished","/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃt/","adj.","卓越的、著名的","We welcome our distinguished guests tonight.","今晚我們歡迎各位貴賓。"],["noteworthy","/ˈnoʊtwɜːrði/","adj.","值得注意的","The report highlights several noteworthy trends.","這份報告強調了幾個值得注意的趨勢。"],["hesitant","/ˈhezɪtənt/","adj.","猶豫的","Some residents were hesitant to support the plan.","一些居民對支持該計畫有所猶豫。"],["advantageous","/ˌædvənˈteɪdʒəs/","adj.","有利的","The new location is advantageous for commuters.","新地點對通勤者很有利。"],["drastic","/ˈdræstɪk/","adj.","激烈的、大幅的","The city took drastic measures to save water.","市府採取大幅措施來節約用水。"],["consecutive","/kənˈsekjətɪv/","adj.","連續的","Sales have risen for five consecutive months.","銷售額已連續五個月上升。"],["biannual","/baɪˈænjuəl/","adj.","一年兩次的","The biannual health fair takes place in spring and fall.","一年兩次的健康博覽會在春季與秋季舉行。"],["outnumber","/ˌaʊtˈnʌmbər/","v.","數量上超過","Female readers outnumber male readers two to one.","女性讀者的人數是男性的兩倍。"],["intensify","/ɪnˈtensɪfaɪ/","v.","加強、加劇","The storm is expected to intensify overnight.","暴風雨預計將在夜間增強。"],["endeavor","/ɪnˈdevər/","v./n.","努力、盡力","We endeavor to answer all inquiries within a day.","我們盡力在一天內回覆所有詢問。"],["allocate","/ˈæləkeɪt/","v.","分配（資源）","We allocated more funds to research.","我們把更多資金分配給研發。"],["allocation","/ˌæləˈkeɪʃən/","n.","分配","The budget allocation was approved.","預算分配已核准。"],["amend","/əˈmend/","v.","修訂","The contract was amended to include a new clause.","合約修訂後加入一條新條款。"],["amendment","/əˈmendmənt/","n.","修正案、修訂","Please review the amendment to the agreement.","請審閱協議的修訂內容。"],["clause","/klɔːz/","n.","條款","This clause covers late payments.","這一條款涵蓋逾期付款。"],["stipulate","/ˈstɪpjuleɪt/","v.","規定、明定","The contract stipulates a 30-day notice period.","合約規定須提前 30 天通知。"],["binding","/ˈbaɪndɪŋ/","adj.","有約束力的","This agreement is legally binding.","這份協議具法律效力。"],["void","/vɔɪd/","adj.","無效的","The warranty is void if the seal is broken.","封條破損則保固失效。"],["waive","/weɪv/","v.","放棄；免除","We will waive the delivery fee this time.","這次我們免收運費。"],["exempt","/ɪɡˈzempt/","adj.","豁免的","Small businesses are exempt from this tax.","小型企業免繳此稅。"],["levy","/ˈlevi/","v./n.","徵收（稅）","The government levied a tax on imports.","政府對進口品課稅。"],["tariff","/ˈtærɪf/","n.","關稅","New tariffs raised the cost of steel.","新關稅讓鋼材成本上升。"],["surcharge","/ˈsɝːtʃɑːrdʒ/","n.","附加費","A fuel surcharge has been added.","已加收燃油附加費。"],["remittance","/rɪˈmɪtns/","n.","匯款","Please send your remittance by bank transfer.","請以銀行轉帳匯款。"],["reimbursement","/ˌriːɪmˈbɝːsmənt/","n.","報銷、退款","Submit receipts for reimbursement.","請提交收據以申請報銷。"],["expenditure","/ɪkˈspendɪtʃɚ/","n.","支出","Capital expenditure rose by 8%.","資本支出增加了 8%。"],["fiscal year","/ˌfɪskl ˈjɪr/","phr.","會計年度","Our fiscal year ends in March.","我們的會計年度在三月結束。"],["dividend","/ˈdɪvɪdend/","n.","股利","Shareholders will receive a dividend.","股東將獲得股利。"],["asset","/ˈæset/","n.","資產","Our people are our greatest asset.","員工是我們最大的資產。"],["equity","/ˈekwəti/","n.","股權；權益","The investor bought a 20% equity stake.","投資人買下兩成股權。"],["collateral","/kəˈlætərəl/","n.","擔保品","The bank asked for collateral for the loan.","銀行要求貸款擔保品。"],["creditor","/ˈkredɪtɚ/","n.","債權人","The company owes money to several creditors.","公司欠了好幾個債權人錢。"],["insolvent","/ɪnˈsɑːlvənt/","adj.","無力償債的","The supplier became insolvent last year.","那家供應商去年無力償債。"],["bankrupt","/ˈbæŋkrʌpt/","adj.","破產的","The retailer went bankrupt.","那家零售商破產了。"],["deficit","/ˈdefɪsɪt/","n.","赤字","The company reported a deficit this quarter.","公司本季呈現虧損。"],["surplus","/ˈsɝːplʌs/","n.","盈餘、過剩","We have a surplus of raw materials.","我們原料過剩。"],["projection","/prəˈdʒekʃən/","n.","預估","Sales projections for next year are optimistic.","明年銷售預估樂觀。"],["benchmark","/ˈbentʃmɑːrk/","n.","基準","We use last year's results as a benchmark.","我們以去年的成果為基準。"],["metric","/ˈmetrɪk/","n.","衡量指標","Customer retention is a key metric.","顧客留存率是關鍵指標。"],["yield","/jiːld/","v./n.","產生；收益","The investment yielded a 6% return.","這筆投資產生 6% 的報酬。"],["venture","/ˈventʃɚ/","n.","事業；冒險","The joint venture was a success.","這個合資事業很成功。"],["entrepreneur","/ˌɑːntrəprəˈnɝː/","n.","創業家","She is a successful entrepreneur.","她是成功的創業家。"],["conglomerate","/kənˈɡlɑːmərət/","n.","企業集團","The conglomerate owns hotels and airlines.","這個集團擁有飯店和航空公司。"],["affiliate","/əˈfɪliət/","n.","關係企業","The product is sold through our affiliates.","產品透過關係企業銷售。"],["franchise","/ˈfræntʃaɪz/","n.","加盟（權）","He bought a coffee shop franchise.","他買下一家咖啡店加盟權。"],["divest","/daɪˈvest/","v.","撤資、出售（部門）","The firm divested its printing business.","公司出售了印刷部門。"],["restructure","/ˌriːˈstrʌktʃɚ/","v.","重整","The company is restructuring its sales team.","公司正在重整業務團隊。"],["downsize","/ˈdaʊnsaɪz/","v.","縮編","The firm downsized by 10% last year.","公司去年縮編一成。"],["layoff","/ˈleɪɔːf/","n.","裁員","There were layoffs at the factory.","工廠有裁員。"],["lay off","/ˌleɪ ˈɔːf/","phr.","裁員、解僱","They laid off 50 workers.","他們裁了 50 名員工。"],["terminate","/ˈtɝːmɪneɪt/","v.","終止","Either party may terminate the contract.","任一方都可終止合約。"],["succession","/səkˈseʃən/","n.","繼任、接班","The board discussed succession planning.","董事會討論接班計畫。"],["successor","/səkˈsesɚ/","n.","繼任者","Who will be the CEO's successor?","誰會接任執行長？"],["predecessor","/ˈpredəsesɚ/","n.","前任","My predecessor left detailed notes.","我的前任留下詳細的筆記。"],["incumbent","/ɪnˈkʌmbənt/","n.","現任者","The incumbent manager will stay until June.","現任經理會留到六月。"],["tenure","/ˈtenjɚ/","n.","任期","During his tenure, sales doubled.","他在任期間業績翻倍。"],["compensation","/ˌkɑːmpenˈseɪʃən/","n.","薪酬；賠償","The compensation package includes stock options.","薪酬方案包含股票選擇權。"],["remuneration","/rɪˌmjuːnəˈreɪʃən/","n.","報酬","Remuneration will depend on experience.","報酬依經驗而定。"],["pension","/ˈpenʃən/","n.","退休金","Employees contribute to a pension plan.","員工提撥退休金計畫。"],["entitled to","/ɪnˈtaɪtld tuː/","phr.","有權得到","Staff are entitled to 14 days of leave.","員工享有 14 天休假。"],["leave of absence","/ˌliːv əv ˈæbsəns/","phr.","留職停薪、請假","She took a leave of absence to study.","她請長假去進修。"],["grievance","/ˈɡriːvəns/","n.","申訴、不滿","Employees can file a grievance with HR.","員工可以向人資提出申訴。"],["disciplinary","/ˈdɪsəplɪneri/","adj.","紀律的、懲戒的","Disciplinary action may be taken.","可能會採取懲處。"],["morale","/məˈræl/","n.","士氣","The bonus boosted staff morale.","獎金提振了員工士氣。"],["retention","/rɪˈtenʃən/","n.","留住（人才、顧客）","Employee retention is a top priority.","留住員工是首要任務。"],["turnover","/ˈtɝːnoʊvɚ/","n.","人員流動率；營業額","The company has a high staff turnover.","這家公司員工流動率高。"],["headhunter","/ˈhedhʌntɚ/","n.","獵人頭","A headhunter contacted me about a job.","有個獵人頭聯絡我談工作。"],["credentials","/krəˈdenʃlz/","n.","資歷、證書","Please verify the candidate's credentials.","請核實應徵者的資歷。"],["proficient","/prəˈfɪʃnt/","adj.","精通的","Applicants must be proficient in Excel.","應徵者須精通 Excel。"],["proficiency","/prəˈfɪʃnsi/","n.","熟練度","English proficiency is required.","需要具備英語能力。"],["aptitude","/ˈæptɪtuːd/","n.","天資、才能","She has an aptitude for numbers.","她對數字很有天分。"],["meticulous","/məˈtɪkjələs/","adj.","一絲不苟的","He is meticulous about details.","他對細節一絲不苟。"],["diligent","/ˈdɪlɪdʒənt/","adj.","勤勉的","She is a diligent worker.","她工作很勤奮。"],["versatile","/ˈvɝːsətl/","adj.","多才多藝的；多用途的","This tool is very versatile.","這工具用途很廣。"],["resourceful","/rɪˈsɔːrsfl/","adj.","機智的、有辦法的","We need a resourceful project manager.","我們需要一個很有辦法的專案經理。"],["conscientious","/ˌkɑːnʃiˈenʃəs/","adj.","認真負責的","She is conscientious and reliable.","她認真又可靠。"],["punctual","/ˈpʌŋktʃuəl/","adj.","準時的","Please be punctual for the interview.","面試請準時。"],["courteous","/ˈkɝːtiəs/","adj.","有禮貌的","Our staff are always courteous.","我們員工總是很有禮貌。"],["prompt","/prɑːmpt/","adj.","迅速的","Thank you for your prompt reply.","謝謝您迅速回覆。"],["cordially","/ˈkɔːrdʒəli/","adv.","誠摯地","You are cordially invited to our opening.","誠摯邀請您參加我們的開幕。"],["hereby","/ˌhɪrˈbaɪ/","adv.","特此","We hereby confirm your order.","特此確認您的訂單。"],["herewith","/ˌhɪrˈwɪð/","adv.","隨函","Please find herewith the signed contract.","隨函附上已簽署的合約。"],["pertaining to","/pɚˈteɪnɪŋ tuː/","phr.","關於","Questions pertaining to billing should go to finance.","帳務相關問題請洽財務部。"],["in compliance with","/ɪn kəmˈplaɪəns wɪð/","phr.","遵照","All products are made in compliance with EU standards.","所有產品皆依歐盟標準製造。"],["in lieu of","/ɪn ˈluː əv/","phr.","代替","Staff may take time off in lieu of overtime pay.","員工可用補休代替加班費。"],["pursuant to","/pɚˈsuːənt tuː/","phr.","依據","Pursuant to our agreement, payment is due now.","依據我們的協議，款項現已到期。"],["contingent on","/kənˈtɪndʒənt ɑːn/","phr.","取決於","The deal is contingent on board approval.","這筆交易取決於董事會是否核准。"],["subject to","/ˈsʌbdʒekt tuː/","phr.","以…為條件；可能受到","Prices are subject to change without notice.","價格如有變動，恕不另行通知。"],["contingency","/kənˈtɪndʒənsi/","n.","意外事件、應變","We have a contingency plan for power outages.","我們有停電的應變計畫。"],["mitigate risk","/ˌmɪtɪɡeɪt ˈrɪsk/","phr.","降低風險","Insurance helps mitigate risk.","保險有助於降低風險。"],["viable","/ˈvaɪəbl/","adj.","可行的","We need a commercially viable product.","我們需要在商業上可行的產品。"],["saturated","/ˈsætʃəreɪtɪd/","adj.","飽和的","The smartphone market is saturated.","智慧型手機市場已飽和。"],["niche","/niːtʃ/","n./adj.","利基（市場）","They focus on a niche market.","他們專注於利基市場。"],["penetrate","/ˈpenɪtreɪt/","v.","打入（市場）","We hope to penetrate the Japanese market.","我們希望打入日本市場。"],["leverage","/ˈlevərɪdʒ/","v./n.","善用；影響力","We can leverage our brand to sell more.","我們可以善用品牌提升銷量。"],["capitalize on","/ˈkæpɪtəlaɪz ɑːn/","phr.","利用（機會）","We should capitalize on this trend.","我們應該把握這個趨勢。"],["diversify","/daɪˈvɝːsɪfaɪ/","v.","多元化","The company diversified into healthcare.","公司跨足醫療業以多元發展。"],["innovative","/ˈɪnəveɪtɪv/","adj.","創新的","They have an innovative design.","他們的設計很創新。"],["innovation","/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃən/","n.","創新","Innovation drives our growth.","創新推動我們的成長。"],["prototype","/ˈproʊtətaɪp/","n.","原型","The engineers built a prototype.","工程師做出了原型。"],["patent","/ˈpætnt/","n.","專利","The company holds a patent for this design.","公司擁有這項設計的專利。"],["trademark","/ˈtreɪdmɑːrk/","n.","商標","The logo is a registered trademark.","這個標誌是註冊商標。"],["infringe","/ɪnˈfrɪndʒ/","v.","侵犯（權利）","The product infringes on our patent.","那項產品侵犯我們的專利。"],["proprietary","/prəˈpraɪəteri/","adj.","專有的","We use proprietary software.","我們用自家專有的軟體。"],["obsolete","/ˌɑːbsəˈliːt/","adj.","過時的、淘汰的","This model is now obsolete.","這個型號已經淘汰。"],["cutting-edge","/ˌkʌtɪŋ ˈedʒ/","adj.","最先進的","We use cutting-edge technology.","我們使用最先進的技術。"],["state-of-the-art","/ˌsteɪt əv ði ˈɑːrt/","adj.","最先進的","The lab has state-of-the-art equipment.","實驗室有最先進的設備。"],["implementation","/ˌɪmplɪmenˈteɪʃən/","n.","實施","The implementation took six months.","導入花了六個月。"],["integrate","/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/","v.","整合","The two systems will be integrated.","兩個系統將整合。"],["optimize","/ˈɑːptɪmaɪz/","v.","最佳化","We optimized the production schedule.","我們優化了生產排程。"],["automate","/ˈɔːtəmeɪt/","v.","自動化","The warehouse is fully automated.","倉庫完全自動化。"],["outsourcing","/ˈaʊtsɔːrsɪŋ/","n.","外包","Outsourcing reduced our costs.","外包降低了我們的成本。"],["bottleneck","/ˈbɑːtlnek/","n.","瓶頸","Packaging is the bottleneck in our process.","包裝是我們流程的瓶頸。"],["backlog","/ˈbæklɔːɡ/","n.","積壓（的工作或訂單）","We have a backlog of orders.","我們積壓了一些訂單。"],["procure","/proʊˈkjʊr/","v.","採購、取得","We procure parts from three countries.","我們向三個國家採購零件。"],["tender","/ˈtendɚ/","n.","投標","The city invited tenders for the project.","市政府為這個案子招標。"],["bid","/bɪd/","n./v.","出價、投標","Our bid was the lowest.","我們的標價最低。"],["specifications","/ˌspesɪfɪˈkeɪʃənz/","n.","規格書","The product must meet the specifications.","產品必須符合規格。"],["consignment","/kənˈsaɪnmənt/","n.","託運貨物；寄售","The consignment arrived damaged.","這批託運貨物到貨時有損壞。"],["adjourn","/əˈdʒɝːn/","v.","休會、延會","The meeting was adjourned until Monday.","會議延到週一再開。"],["convene","/kənˈviːn/","v.","召開","The board will convene next week.","董事會將於下週召開。"],["deliberate","/dɪˈlɪbəreɪt/","v.","仔細考慮、商議","The committee deliberated for hours.","委員會商議了好幾個小時。"],["consensus","/kənˈsensəs/","n.","共識","We reached a consensus on the budget.","我們在預算上達成共識。"],["quorum","/ˈkwɔːrəm/","n.","法定人數","The vote was delayed due to lack of a quorum.","因未達法定人數，投票延後。"],["abstain","/əbˈsteɪn/","v.","棄權；戒絕","Two members abstained from voting.","有兩位成員棄權。"],["ratify","/ˈrætɪfaɪ/","v.","正式批准","The agreement was ratified by both parties.","協議經雙方正式批准。"],["stipend","/ˈstaɪpend/","n.","津貼","Interns receive a monthly stipend.","實習生每月領津貼。"],["honorarium","/ˌɑːnəˈreriəm/","n.","酬金","Speakers receive a small honorarium.","講者會拿到一點酬金。"],["disburse","/dɪsˈbɝːs/","v.","支付、撥款","Funds will be disbursed next month.","款項將於下個月撥付。"],["accrue","/əˈkruː/","v.","累積","Interest accrues daily.","利息每日累計。"],["amortize","/ˈæmɚtaɪz/","v.","攤銷、分期償還","The cost is amortized over five years.","成本分五年攤銷。"],["depreciation","/dɪˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃən/","n.","折舊","Depreciation reduces the value of equipment.","折舊會降低設備的價值。"],["appraisal","/əˈpreɪzl/","n.","評估、估價","The property appraisal came in high.","房產估價很高。"],["valuation","/ˌvæljuˈeɪʃən/","n.","估值","The startup's valuation reached $1 billion.","這家新創估值達到十億美元。"],["audit trail","/ˈɔːdɪt treɪl/","phr.","稽核紀錄","Keep a clear audit trail of all payments.","所有付款都要保留清楚的稽核紀錄。"],["ledger","/ˈledʒɚ/","n.","帳簿","All expenses are recorded in the ledger.","所有支出都記在帳簿上。"],["receivable","/rɪˈsiːvəbl/","adj./n.","應收的；應收帳款","Accounts receivable have increased.","應收帳款增加了。"],["payable","/ˈpeɪəbl/","adj.","應付的","The invoice is payable within 30 days.","發票須於 30 天內付款。"],["solvency","/ˈsɑːlvənsi/","n.","償債能力","The bank checked the firm's solvency.","銀行查核了公司的償債能力。"],["liquidity","/lɪˈkwɪdəti/","n.","流動性","The company has strong liquidity.","公司流動性很好。"],["volatile","/ˈvɑːlətl/","adj.","波動大的","The stock market is volatile.","股市波動很大。"],["plummet","/ˈplʌmɪt/","v.","暴跌","Profits plummeted after the recall.","召回後利潤暴跌。"],["soar","/sɔːr/","v.","飆升","Demand soared during the holidays.","假期間需求飆升。"],["surge","/sɝːdʒ/","n./v.","激增","There was a surge in online orders.","線上訂單激增。"],["stagnant","/ˈstæɡnənt/","adj.","停滯的","Wages have been stagnant for years.","薪資多年停滯。"],["robust","/roʊˈbʌst/","adj.","強健的","The economy showed robust growth.","經濟成長強勁。"],["sluggish","/ˈslʌɡɪʃ/","adj.","低迷的","Sales were sluggish in the first quarter.","第一季業績低迷。"],["downturn","/ˈdaʊntɝːn/","n.","衰退","Many firms cut costs during the downturn.","景氣衰退時很多公司削減成本。"],["recession","/rɪˈseʃən/","n.","經濟衰退","The country entered a recession.","那個國家進入經濟衰退。"],["inflation","/ɪnˈfleɪʃən/","n.","通貨膨脹","Inflation reached 4% last year.","去年通膨達到 4%。"],["fluctuation","/ˌflʌktʃuˈeɪʃən/","n.","波動","Currency fluctuations affect our profits.","匯率波動影響我們的利潤。"],["exchange rate","/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ reɪt/","phr.","匯率","The exchange rate is favorable now.","現在匯率很有利。"],["outlook","/ˈaʊtlʊk/","n.","前景","The outlook for the industry is positive.","產業前景樂觀。"],["projected","/prəˈdʒektɪd/","adj.","預計的","Projected sales for 2027 are $5 million.","2027 年預計銷售額 500 萬美元。"],["clientele","/ˌklaɪənˈtel/","n.","（全體）顧客","The hotel has a wealthy clientele.","這間飯店的客群很富裕。"],["demographic","/ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/","n.","人口族群","Our target demographic is young adults.","我們的目標族群是年輕人。"],["endorsement","/ɪnˈdɔːrsmənt/","n.","代言；背書","The athlete signed an endorsement deal.","那位運動員簽了代言合約。"],["testimonial","/ˌtestɪˈmoʊniəl/","n.","推薦文、使用者見證","Our website features customer testimonials.","我們網站有顧客推薦文。"],["solicit","/səˈlɪsɪt/","v.","徵求","We are soliciting feedback from users.","我們正在徵求使用者意見。"],["unsolicited","/ˌʌnsəˈlɪsɪtɪd/","adj.","未經請求的","We do not accept unsolicited proposals.","我們不接受主動投遞的提案。"],["patronage","/ˈpætrənɪdʒ/","n.","光顧、惠顧","Thank you for your continued patronage.","感謝您長期惠顧。"],["redeem","/rɪˈdiːm/","v.","兌換","Points can be redeemed for gift cards.","點數可兌換禮物卡。"],["warranty claim","/ˈwɔːrənti kleɪm/","phr.","保固申請","You can file a warranty claim online.","可以線上申請保固。"],["recall","/ˈriːkɔːl/","n./v.","（產品）召回","The company issued a recall of 10,000 heaters.","公司召回了一萬台暖爐。"],["liable","/ˈlaɪəbl/","adj.","負法律責任的","The company is not liable for lost items.","公司對遺失物品不負責。"],["indemnify","/ɪnˈdemnɪfaɪ/","v.","賠償","The supplier agrees to indemnify us for losses.","供應商同意賠償我們的損失。"],["dispute","/dɪˈspjuːt/","n./v.","爭議","The dispute was settled out of court.","爭議在庭外和解。"],["arbitration","/ˌɑːrbɪˈtreɪʃən/","n.","仲裁","The case went to arbitration.","這個案子進入仲裁。"],["litigation","/ˌlɪtɪˈɡeɪʃən/","n.","訴訟","We want to avoid costly litigation.","我們想避免昂貴的訴訟。"],["settlement","/ˈsetlmənt/","n.","和解；結算","Both sides agreed to a settlement.","雙方同意和解。"],["breach","/briːtʃ/","n./v.","違反（合約）","Late delivery is a breach of contract.","延遲交貨屬於違約。"],["counterpart","/ˈkaʊntɚpɑːrt/","n.","對應的人、對口","I met my Japanese counterpart in Tokyo.","我在東京見了日方的對口窗口。"],["liaison","/ˈliːəzɑːn/","n.","聯絡人；聯繫","She acts as a liaison between the two teams.","她是兩個團隊之間的聯絡窗口。"],["delegate","/ˈdelɪɡeɪt/","v./n.","委派；代表","A good manager knows how to delegate.","好主管懂得授權。"],["delegation","/ˌdelɪˈɡeɪʃən/","n.","代表團；授權","A delegation from Germany visited our plant.","德國代表團參觀了我們工廠。"],["itinerant","/aɪˈtɪnərənt/","adj.","巡迴的","He works as an itinerant sales trainer.","他是巡迴各地的業務講師。"],["relocation","/ˌriːloʊˈkeɪʃən/","n.","搬遷","The company paid for my relocation.","公司負擔了我的搬遷費用。"],["telecommute","/ˈtelɪkəmjuːt/","v.","遠距上班","Many staff telecommute two days a week.","很多員工每週遠距上班兩天。"],["remote work","/rɪˌmoʊt ˈwɝːk/","phr.","遠端工作","Remote work is now common.","遠端工作現在很普遍。"],["flextime","/ˈflekstaɪm/","n.","彈性工時","The company offers flextime.","公司提供彈性工時。"],["workforce","/ˈwɝːkfɔːrs/","n.","勞動力、全體員工","Women make up half of our workforce.","女性占我們員工的一半。"],["staffing","/ˈstæfɪŋ/","n.","人員配置","We have staffing problems on weekends.","週末人手不足。"],["understaffed","/ˌʌndɚˈstæft/","adj.","人手不足的","The store is understaffed today.","店裡今天人手不足。"],["payroll","/ˈpeɪroʊl/","n.","薪資名冊；薪資","Payroll is processed on the 25th.","薪資在 25 號處理。"],["deduction","/dɪˈdʌkʃən/","n.","扣除額","Tax deductions are shown on your pay slip.","扣稅金額列在薪資單上。"],["withhold","/wɪθˈhoʊld/","v.","扣留、保留","Taxes are withheld from your salary.","稅款會從薪資中扣繳。"],["gross","/ɡroʊs/","adj.","總的、毛的","Gross revenue rose by 9%.","總營收成長 9%。"],["net","/net/","adj.","淨的","Net profit fell slightly.","淨利略微下降。"],["margin","/ˈmɑːrdʒɪn/","n.","利潤率；邊緣","Our profit margins are getting smaller.","我們的利潤率越來越低。"],["overhead","/ˈoʊvɚhed/","n.","管銷費用","Moving online cut our overhead costs.","轉到線上降低了管銷成本。"],["feasibility study","/ˌfiːzəˈbɪləti ˌstʌdi/","phr.","可行性研究","We ordered a feasibility study for the new plant.","我們委託做新廠的可行性研究。"],["pilot","/ˈpaɪlət/","adj./n.","試行的","We launched a pilot program in two stores.","我們在兩家店試行這個方案。"],["phase","/feɪz/","n.","階段","The first phase of the project is complete.","專案第一階段已完成。"],["milestone","/ˈmaɪlstoʊn/","n.","里程碑","Reaching 1 million users was a milestone.","突破百萬用戶是個里程碑。"],["deliverable","/dɪˈlɪvərəbl/","n.","交付成果","The main deliverable is a final report.","主要交付成果是一份期末報告。"],["scope","/skoʊp/","n.","範圍","That task is outside the scope of the project.","那項工作不在專案範圍內。"],["oversight","/ˈoʊvɚsaɪt/","n.","疏忽；監督","The error was due to an oversight.","這個錯誤是疏忽造成的。"],["discrepancies","/dɪˈskrepənsiz/","n.","不一致之處","Please report any discrepancies immediately.","發現任何不符請立即回報。"],["rectify","/ˈrektɪfaɪ/","v.","糾正","We will rectify the error right away.","我們會立刻更正錯誤。"],["expedient","/ɪkˈspiːdiənt/","adj.","權宜的、方便的","It's more expedient to email the forms.","用 email 寄表格比較方便。"],["imperative","/ɪmˈperətɪv/","adj.","必要的、緊急的","It is imperative that we meet the deadline.","我們務必趕上期限。"],["paramount","/ˈpærəmaʊnt/","adj.","最重要的","Customer safety is paramount.","顧客安全最重要。"],["pivotal","/ˈpɪvətl/","adj.","關鍵的","She played a pivotal role in the deal.","她在這筆交易中扮演關鍵角色。"],["instrumental","/ˌɪnstrəˈmentl/","adj.","起重要作用的","He was instrumental in opening the Asian market.","他對打開亞洲市場功不可沒。"],["inadvertently","/ˌɪnədˈvɝːtntli/","adv.","不小心地","I inadvertently deleted the file.","我不小心刪了檔案。"],["tentatively","/ˈtentətɪvli/","adv.","暫定地","The launch is tentatively set for May.","上市暫定五月。"],["subsequently","/ˈsʌbsɪkwəntli/","adv.","隨後","The product was tested and subsequently approved.","產品經過測試後隨即獲准。"],["consequently","/ˈkɑːnsəkwentli/","adv.","因此","Demand fell; consequently, prices dropped.","需求下降，因此價格下跌。"],["accordingly","/əˈkɔːrdɪŋli/","adv.","相應地","Prices will be adjusted accordingly.","價格將相應調整。"],["henceforth","/ˌhensˈfɔːrθ/","adv.","今後","Henceforth, all reports must be submitted online.","今後所有報告都須線上提交。"],["whereby","/werˈbaɪ/","adv.","藉此、憑此","We set up a system whereby staff can report issues.","我們建立了一套讓員工回報問題的制度。"],["aforementioned","/əˈfɔːrmenʃənd/","adj.","前述的","The aforementioned changes take effect today.","上述變更今天生效。"],["foregoing","/ˈfɔːrɡoʊɪŋ/","adj.","前述的","Based on the foregoing, we recommend option B.","基於上述，我們建議方案 B。"],["undertake","/ˌʌndɚˈteɪk/","v.","承擔、著手","The company undertook a major expansion.","公司著手進行大規模擴張。"],["undergo","/ˌʌndɚˈɡoʊ/","v.","經歷、接受","The building will undergo renovation.","大樓將進行整修。"],["uphold","/ʌpˈhoʊld/","v.","維護、維持","We uphold the highest standards.","我們堅守最高標準。"],["enforce","/ɪnˈfɔːrs/","v.","執行（法規）","The rules are strictly enforced.","規定嚴格執行。"],["spearhead","/ˈspɪrhed/","v.","帶頭、主導","He spearheaded the new marketing campaign.","他主導了新的行銷活動。"],["streamlined","/ˈstriːmlaɪnd/","adj.","精簡的","We now have a streamlined approval process.","我們現在有精簡的審核流程。"],["scrutinize","/ˈskruːtənaɪz/","v.","仔細審查","The lawyers scrutinized every clause.","律師仔細審查每一條款。"],["verify","/ˈverɪfaɪ/","v.","核實","Please verify your email address.","請驗證您的 email 地址。"],["validate","/ˈvælɪdeɪt/","v.","驗證；確認有效","Parking tickets can be validated at the front desk.","停車券可在櫃台蓋章折抵。"],["substantiate","/səbˈstænʃieɪt/","v.","證實","Can you substantiate these claims?","你能證實這些說法嗎？"],["disclose","/dɪsˈkloʊz/","v.","透露、揭露","The price of the deal was not disclosed.","這筆交易的金額沒有公開。"],["disclosure","/dɪsˈkloʊʒɚ/","n.","揭露","Financial disclosure is required by law.","法律規定必須揭露財務資訊。"],["transparency","/trænsˈpærənsi/","n.","透明度","Investors want more transparency.","投資人希望更透明。"],["accountability","/əˌkaʊntəˈbɪləti/","n.","問責、負責","We need more accountability in management.","管理層需要更多問責。"],["ethical","/ˈeθɪkl/","adj.","合乎道德的","We only work with ethical suppliers.","我們只跟有道德的供應商合作。"],["integrity","/ɪnˈteɡrəti/","n.","誠信","Integrity is one of our core values.","誠信是我們的核心價值之一。"],["adept","/əˈdept/","adj.","熟練的","She is adept at handling difficult clients.","她很擅長應付難搞的客戶。"],["astute","/əˈstuːt/","adj.","精明的","He is an astute negotiator.","他是精明的談判者。"],["prudent","/ˈpruːdnt/","adj.","謹慎的","It would be prudent to wait.","等一等會比較謹慎。"],["judicious","/dʒuˈdɪʃəs/","adj.","明智的","We made judicious use of our budget.","我們明智地運用預算。"],["pragmatic","/præɡˈmætɪk/","adj.","務實的","We need a pragmatic approach.","我們需要務實的做法。"],["comprehensive","/ˌkɑːmprɪˈhensɪv/","adj.","全面的","We offer comprehensive insurance.","我們提供全面的保險。"],["exhaustive","/ɪɡˈzɔːstɪv/","adj.","詳盡的","The report includes an exhaustive list of costs.","報告列出了詳盡的費用清單。"],["concise","/kənˈsaɪs/","adj.","簡潔的","Keep your summary concise.","摘要請簡潔。"],["succinct","/səkˈsɪŋkt/","adj.","簡明扼要的","Her explanation was clear and succinct.","她的說明清楚又簡潔。"],["ambiguous","/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/","adj.","模稜兩可的","The wording of the contract is ambiguous.","合約的措辭模稜兩可。"],["explicit","/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/","adj.","明確的","Please give explicit instructions.","請給明確的指示。"],["implicit","/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/","adj.","隱含的","There was an implicit agreement.","雙方有默契。"],["stringent","/ˈstrɪndʒənt/","adj.","嚴格的","The factory follows stringent safety rules.","工廠遵守嚴格的安全規定。"],["lenient","/ˈliːniənt/","adj.","寬鬆的","The return policy is quite lenient.","退貨規定相當寬鬆。"],["rigorous","/ˈrɪɡərəs/","adj.","嚴謹的","All products undergo rigorous testing.","所有產品都經過嚴格測試。"],["nominal","/ˈnɑːmɪnl/","adj.","象徵性的、極少的","There is a nominal fee for parking.","停車只收象徵性的費用。"],["exorbitant","/ɪɡˈzɔːrbɪtənt/","adj.","過高的","The hotel charged exorbitant prices.","那家飯店收費貴得離譜。"],["prohibitive","/proʊˈhɪbətɪv/","adj.","貴到讓人卻步的","The cost of the system is prohibitive.","那套系統貴得讓人負擔不起。"],["negligible","/ˈneɡlɪdʒəbl/","adj.","可忽略的","The difference in price is negligible.","價差可以忽略。"],["marginal","/ˈmɑːrdʒɪnl/","adj.","些微的","There was only a marginal improvement.","只有些微改善。"],["substantially","/səbˈstænʃəli/","adv.","大幅地","Costs have increased substantially.","成本大幅增加。"],["markedly","/ˈmɑːrkɪdli/","adv.","明顯地","Sales improved markedly after the campaign.","活動後業績明顯改善。"],["exceedingly","/ɪkˈsiːdɪŋli/","adv.","極其","The project was exceedingly difficult.","這個專案極其困難。"],["predominantly","/prɪˈdɑːmɪnəntli/","adv.","主要地","Our customers are predominantly young.","我們的客戶主要是年輕人。"],["invariably","/ɪnˈveriəbli/","adv.","總是、一律","The train is invariably late.","這班火車總是誤點。"],["intermittently","/ˌɪntɚˈmɪtəntli/","adv.","斷斷續續地","The system failed intermittently.","系統斷斷續續故障。"],["simultaneously","/ˌsaɪmlˈteɪniəsli/","adv.","同時地","The product launched simultaneously in five countries.","產品在五國同步上市。"],["provisionally","/prəˈvɪʒənəli/","adv.","暫時地、臨時地","The date has been provisionally set.","日期暫時定下了。"],["retroactively","/ˌretroʊˈæktɪvli/","adv.","追溯地","The pay raise applies retroactively from January.","加薪從一月起追溯生效。"],["inaugurate","/ɪˈnɔːɡjəreɪt/","v.","為…舉行開幕；就職","The mayor inaugurated the new bridge.","市長為新橋主持啟用。"],["commemorate","/kəˈmeməreɪt/","v.","紀念","The event commemorates our 50th anniversary.","活動紀念公司創立 50 週年。"],["anniversary","/ˌænɪˈvɝːsəri/","n.","週年紀念","We are celebrating our tenth anniversary.","我們正在慶祝十週年。"],["gala","/ˈɡeɪlə/","n.","盛會","The charity gala raised $2 million.","慈善晚會募得兩百萬美元。"],["philanthropy","/fɪˈlænθrəpi/","n.","慈善事業","The founder is known for his philanthropy.","創辦人以慈善事業聞名。"],["benefactor","/ˈbenɪfæktɚ/","n.","捐助人","The library was funded by a generous benefactor.","圖書館由一位慷慨的捐助者出資。"],["endowment","/ɪnˈdaʊmənt/","n.","捐贈基金","The university has a large endowment.","這所大學有大筆捐贈基金。"],["grant","/ɡrænt/","n./v.","補助金；授予","We received a government grant for research.","我們獲得政府研究補助。"],["subsidy","/ˈsʌbsədi/","n.","補貼","Farmers receive a subsidy from the state.","農民領有政府補貼。"],["commission","/kəˈmɪʃən/","n./v.","佣金；委託","Sales staff earn a 5% commission.","業務人員可抽 5% 佣金。"],["quota","/ˈkwoʊtə/","n.","配額、業績目標","He exceeded his sales quota.","他超過了業績目標。"],["exceed","/ɪkˈsiːd/","v.","超過","Demand exceeded our expectations.","需求超出我們的預期。"],["surpass","/sɚˈpæs/","v.","超越","This year's sales surpassed last year's.","今年業績超越去年。"],["outperform","/ˌaʊtpɚˈfɔːrm/","v.","表現優於","Our new model outperforms the competition.","我們的新款表現勝過競品。"],["underperform","/ˌʌndɚpɚˈfɔːrm/","v.","表現不如預期","The Asian branch underperformed last quarter.","亞洲分公司上季表現不佳。"],["reallocate","/ˌriːˈæləkeɪt/","v.","重新分配","We reallocated staff to the busy branch.","我們把人力重新調到忙碌的分店。"],["curtail","/kɝːˈteɪl/","v.","削減","We had to curtail travel expenses.","我們必須削減差旅費。"],["slash","/slæʃ/","v.","大幅削減","The store slashed prices by 50%.","店家價格砍半。"],["augment","/ɔːɡˈment/","v.","增加、擴大","We hired temps to augment our staff.","我們請臨時工來擴充人力。"],["bolster","/ˈboʊlstɚ/","v.","加強、支撐","The new product bolstered our sales.","新產品撐起了我們的業績。"],["replenish","/rɪˈplenɪʃ/","v.","補充","Please replenish the paper supply.","請補充紙張。"],["deplete","/dɪˈpliːt/","v.","耗盡","Our stock of masks is depleted.","口罩庫存已經用完。"],["dwindle","/ˈdwɪndl/","v.","逐漸減少","Our savings dwindled during the slow season.","淡季時我們的存款逐漸減少。"],["escalate","/ˈeskəleɪt/","v.","升級、擴大","If the problem escalates, call the manager.","問題擴大的話就打給經理。"],["expedited","/ˈekspədaɪtɪd/","adj.","加速處理的","We offer expedited processing for a fee.","付費可加速處理。"],["pending","/ˈpendɪŋ/","adj./prep.","待決的；在…之前","The deal is pending approval.","這筆交易正等待核准。"],["settle","/ˈsetl/","v.","結清；解決","Please settle your bill before leaving.","離開前請結帳。"],["default","/dɪˈfɔːlt/","n./v.","違約、拖欠；預設","The borrower defaulted on the loan.","借款人拖欠貸款。"],["foreclose","/fɔːrˈkloʊz/","v.","取消贖回權（法拍）","The bank foreclosed on the property.","銀行把那間房產法拍了。"],["mortgage","/ˈmɔːrɡɪdʒ/","n.","房貸","They took out a 20-year mortgage.","他們申請了 20 年房貸。"],["lessee","/leˈsiː/","n.","承租人","The lessee is responsible for repairs.","承租人負責維修。"],["lessor","/leˈsɔːr/","n.","出租人","The lessor must give 60 days' notice.","出租人須提前 60 天通知。"],["premises","/ˈpremɪsɪz/","n.","營業場所","Smoking is not allowed on the premises.","場所內禁止吸菸。"],["zoning","/ˈzoʊnɪŋ/","n.","分區規劃","Zoning laws prevent factories here.","分區法規禁止在此設廠。"],["occupancy","/ˈɑːkjəpənsi/","n.","入住率；使用","Hotel occupancy reached 90%.","飯店入住率達九成。"],["refurbish","/ˌriːˈfɝːbɪʃ/","v.","翻新","The lobby was recently refurbished.","大廳最近翻新過。"],["retrofit","/ˈretroʊfɪt/","v.","改裝（加裝新設備）","We retrofitted the old building with solar panels.","我們在舊大樓加裝了太陽能板。"],["fixture","/ˈfɪkstʃɚ/","n.","固定裝置","The rent includes all light fixtures.","租金包含所有燈具。"],["appliance","/əˈplaɪəns/","n.","家電","The apartment comes with new appliances.","公寓附新家電。"],["requisition","/ˌrekwɪˈzɪʃən/","n.","請購單","Submit a requisition for new supplies.","新的用品請填請購單。"],["manifest","/ˈmænɪfest/","n.","貨單、艙單","Check the shipping manifest carefully.","仔細核對貨運艙單。"],["customs clearance","/ˈkʌstəmz ˌklɪrəns/","phr.","清關","Customs clearance took three days.","清關花了三天。"],["bill of lading","/ˌbɪl əv ˈleɪdɪŋ/","phr.","提單","The bill of lading was sent to the buyer.","提單已寄給買方。"],["perishable","/ˈperɪʃəbl/","adj.","易腐壞的","Perishable goods must be kept cold.","易腐商品必須冷藏。"],["fragile","/ˈfrædʒl/","adj.","易碎的","This box contains fragile items.","這箱裝有易碎品。"],["courier service","/ˈkʊriɚ ˌsɝːvɪs/","phr.","快遞服務","We use an express courier service.","我們使用快遞服務。"],["proofread","/ˈpruːfriːd/","v.","校對","Please proofread the brochure before printing.","印刷前請校對簡介。"],["collate","/kəˈleɪt/","v.","整理、核對","Please collate the reports by region.","請把報告依地區整理。"],["compile","/kəmˈpaɪl/","v.","彙編","She compiled a list of potential clients.","她彙整了一份潛在客戶名單。"],["tabulate","/ˈtæbjuleɪt/","v.","製成表格","The results were tabulated by the team.","團隊把結果整理成表格。"],["excerpt","/ˈeksɝːpt/","n.","摘錄","Here is an excerpt from the annual report.","以下是年報的摘錄。"],["memorandum","/ˌmeməˈrændəm/","n.","備忘錄","A memorandum was sent to all staff.","已寄送備忘錄給全體員工。"],["addendum","/əˈdendəm/","n.","附錄、補充條款","Please sign the addendum to the contract.","請簽署合約的補充條款。"],["appendix","/əˈpendɪks/","n.","附錄","The data is in the appendix.","資料在附錄裡。"],["itemized","/ˈaɪtəmaɪzd/","adj.","逐項列出的","Please send an itemized bill.","請寄逐項列明的帳單。"],["verbatim","/vɚˈbeɪtɪm/","adv.","逐字地","He repeated the instructions verbatim.","他逐字重複了指示。"],["confidentiality","/ˌkɑːnfɪdenʃiˈæləti/","n.","保密","You must sign a confidentiality agreement.","你必須簽保密協議。"],["nondisclosure","/ˌnɑːndɪsˈkloʊʒɚ/","n.","不揭露、保密","Both firms signed a nondisclosure agreement.","兩家公司簽了保密協議。"],["authentication","/ɔːˌθentɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","身分驗證","Two-step authentication is required.","需要兩步驟驗證。"],["encryption","/ɪnˈkrɪpʃən/","n.","加密","All data is protected by encryption.","所有資料都經加密保護。"],["breach of security","/ˌbriːtʃ əv sɪˈkjʊrəti/","phr.","安全漏洞","A breach of security exposed customer data.","安全漏洞導致客戶資料外洩。"],["compatible","/kəmˈpætəbl/","adj.","相容的","The software is compatible with Mac.","這套軟體與 Mac 相容。"],["interface","/ˈɪntɚfeɪs/","n.","介面","The new interface is easier to use.","新介面比較好用。"],["configure","/kənˈfɪɡjɚ/","v.","設定、配置","IT will configure your laptop.","IT 會幫你設定筆電。"],["deploy","/dɪˈplɔɪ/","v.","部署","The new system will be deployed next month.","新系統下個月上線。"],["glitch","/ɡlɪtʃ/","n.","小故障","A software glitch delayed the payments.","一個軟體小故障延誤了付款。"],["outage","/ˈaʊtɪdʒ/","n.","停電、斷線","A power outage shut down the factory.","停電讓工廠停擺。"],["downtime","/ˈdaʊntaɪm/","n.","停機時間","Scheduled downtime is from 1 to 3 a.m.","預定停機時間是凌晨一點到三點。"],["redundancy","/rɪˈdʌndənsi/","n.","冗餘；（英）裁員","We built redundancy into the network.","我們在網路中設置了備援。"],["scalable","/ˈskeɪləbl/","adj.","可擴充的","We need a scalable solution.","我們需要可擴充的解決方案。"],["sustainable growth","/səˌsteɪnəbl ˈɡroʊθ/","phr.","永續成長","Our goal is sustainable growth.","我們的目標是永續成長。"],["synergy","/ˈsɪnɚdʒi/","n.","綜效","The merger created strong synergies.","合併產生了很強的綜效。"],["paradigm shift","/ˈpærədaɪm ʃɪft/","phr.","典範轉移","AI is causing a paradigm shift in many industries.","AI 正在許多產業造成典範轉移。"],["stakeholder engagement","/ˌsteɪkhoʊldɚ ɪnˈɡeɪdʒmənt/","phr.","利害關係人溝通","Stakeholder engagement is key to success.","與利害關係人溝通是成功關鍵。"],["due diligence","/ˌduː ˈdɪlɪdʒəns/","phr.","盡職調查","We did due diligence before the acquisition.","收購前我們做了盡職調查。"],["turnaround","/ˈtɝːnəraʊnd/","n.","轉虧為盈；處理時間","The new CEO led a remarkable turnaround.","新執行長帶領公司漂亮翻身。"],["turnaround time","/ˈtɝːnəraʊnd taɪm/","phr.","處理所需時間","Our turnaround time is 48 hours.","我們的處理時間是 48 小時。"],["attrition","/əˈtrɪʃən/","n.","自然減員","We'll reduce staff through attrition.","我們會透過自然減員來縮編。"],["severance","/ˈsevərəns/","n.","資遣費","Laid-off workers received severance pay.","被裁員工領到資遣費。"],["arbitrator","/ˈɑːrbɪtreɪtɚ/","n.","仲裁人","An arbitrator will decide the case.","仲裁人會裁決這個案子。"],["plaintiff","/ˈpleɪntɪf/","n.","原告","The plaintiff asked for damages.","原告要求損害賠償。"],["defendant","/dɪˈfendənt/","n.","被告","The defendant denied the claims.","被告否認這些指控。"],["injunction","/ɪnˈdʒʌŋkʃən/","n.","禁令","The court issued an injunction.","法院發出禁令。"],["statute","/ˈstætʃuːt/","n.","法令","The statute protects consumers.","這條法令保護消費者。"],["jurisdiction","/ˌdʒʊrɪsˈdɪkʃən/","n.","管轄權","The case is outside our jurisdiction.","此案不在我們管轄範圍。"],["compliance officer","/kəmˈplaɪəns ˌɔːfɪsɚ/","phr.","法遵主管","The compliance officer reviewed the contract.","法遵主管審閱了合約。"],["regulatory","/ˈreɡjələtɔːri/","adj.","監管的","We need regulatory approval first.","我們需要先取得主管機關核准。"],["precedent","/ˈpresɪdənt/","n.","先例","This case sets a precedent.","這個案例開了先例。"],["conducive","/kənˈduːsɪv/","adj.","有助於…的","The quiet office is conducive to work.","安靜的辦公室有助工作。"],["detrimental to","/ˌdetrɪˈmentl tuː/","phr.","對…有害","The delay was detrimental to our sales.","延誤對我們的業績不利。"],["adverse","/ædˈvɝːs/","adj.","不利的","Adverse weather delayed the shipment.","惡劣天氣延誤了出貨。"],["inclement","/ɪnˈklemənt/","adj.","（天氣）惡劣的","The event was canceled due to inclement weather.","活動因天候不佳取消。"],["unforeseen","/ˌʌnfɔːrˈsiːn/","adj.","未預見的","Due to unforeseen circumstances, the flight was canceled.","因不可預見的情況，班機取消了。"],["at the discretion of","/ət ðə dɪˈskreʃən əv/","phr.","由…決定","Refunds are at the discretion of the manager.","退款與否由經理決定。"],["discretionary","/dɪˈskreʃəneri/","adj.","可自行決定的","Bonuses are discretionary.","獎金由公司酌情發放。"],["in conjunction with","/ɪn kənˈdʒʌŋkʃən wɪð/","phr.","與…一起","The event is held in conjunction with the trade fair.","這場活動與商展同時舉辦。"],["with regard to","/wɪð rɪˈɡɑːrd tuː/","phr.","關於","With regard to your request, we agree.","關於您的請求，我們同意。"],["in the event of","/ɪn ði ɪˈvent əv/","phr.","萬一","In the event of rain, the party will be indoors.","萬一下雨，派對改在室內。"],["on the grounds that","/ɑːn ðə ˈɡraʊndz ðæt/","phr.","基於…理由","The claim was rejected on the grounds that it was late.","申請以逾期為由被駁回。"],["by virtue of","/baɪ ˈvɝːtʃuː əv/","phr.","由於、憑藉","By virtue of his experience, he got the job.","憑著經驗，他得到了這份工作。"],["irrespective of","/ˌɪrɪˈspektɪv əv/","phr.","不論","Everyone gets the same bonus irrespective of rank.","不論職級，大家獎金都一樣。"],["in light of","/ɪn ˈlaɪt əv/","phr.","鑑於","In light of the feedback, we changed the design.","鑑於這些回饋，我們改了設計。"],["to the extent that","/tə ði ɪkˈstent ðæt/","phr.","在…程度上","We will help to the extent that we can.","我們會盡力協助。"],["as a token of","/əz ə ˈtoʊkən əv/","phr.","作為…的表示","Please accept this gift as a token of our thanks.","請收下這份禮物，聊表謝意。"],["reciprocate","/rɪˈsɪprəkeɪt/","v.","回報、互惠","We hope to reciprocate your kindness.","希望能回報您的好意。"],["acknowledge","/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒ/","v.","確認收到；承認","Please acknowledge receipt of this email.","收到這封信請回覆確認。"],["receipt of","/rɪˈsiːt əv/","phr.","收到（某物）","Payment is due upon receipt of the invoice.","收到發票後即須付款。"],["upon request","/əˌpɑːn rɪˈkwest/","phr.","應要求","Samples are available upon request.","樣品可應要求提供。"],["expressly","/ɪkˈspresli/","adv.","明確地","Smoking is expressly prohibited.","嚴格禁止吸菸。"],["duly","/ˈduːli/","adv.","適當地；按時地","The form was duly signed.","表格已依規定簽署。"],["thereafter","/ˌðerˈæftɚ/","adv.","此後","The fee is $10 for the first month and $20 thereafter.","首月 10 元，之後每月 20 元。"],["therein","/ˌðerˈɪn/","adv.","在其中","Read the contract and the terms therein.","請閱讀合約及其中條款。"],["inasmuch as","/ˌɪnəzˈmʌtʃ æz/","phr.","因為、鑑於","Inasmuch as the client agreed, we can proceed.","既然客戶同意了，我們就可以進行。"],["heretofore","/ˌhɪrtəˈfɔːr/","adv.","迄今","Heretofore, all orders were handled by phone.","迄今所有訂單都是電話處理。"],["nonrefundable","/ˌnɑːnrɪˈfʌndəbl/","adj.","不可退款的","The deposit is nonrefundable.","訂金不可退。"],["non-negotiable","/ˌnɑːn nɪˈɡoʊʃiəbl/","adj.","不可商量的","The deadline is non-negotiable.","期限沒有商量的餘地。"]]});
